\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ Conducted JPY Rate Check -Two Dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2012\par 15:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  roiled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Friday following weak U.S. jobs data by conducting so-called rate checks, two traders said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's queries about the latest dollar/yen price was an acceleration of recent warnings on the yen's surge, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan's government view as undermining exporters' strength and thus the domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ's queries to financial institutions briefly caused the dollar to jump half a yen before it came down. This followed disappointing U.S. employment data at 8:30 a.m. EDT which had pushed the dollar down versus the yen.\par \par \uc2 "Yes there was it," one trader said when asked about BOJ queries. This trader and another said that while the BOJ asked for the latest dollar/yen price, it didn't actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by saying 'mine' when told the price.\par \par \uc2 A senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official had no comment. The BOJ couldn't immediately be reached.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate-check is a type of warning ahead of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Earlier in the day in Asia, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister, Jun Azumi, said the government would take decisive steps--which is generally interpreted as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 --if the yen's excessive moves continue.\par \par \uc2 Separately, there had been rumors in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that the U.S. Federal Reserve had likewise checked dollar rates. A New York \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  spokesman declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 --William Kemble-Diaz, Erin McCarthy and Geoffrey Rogow contributed to this story [ 06-01-12 0950ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120601e8610009e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
