\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar falls versus yen, euro after jobs data\b0\par\par\uc2 932 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2012\par 02:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Euro comes off 23-month low vs dollar after dismal U.S. jobs data\par \par \uc2 * Safe-haven yen rises, market wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * U.S. economy adds only 69,000 jobs in May, jobless rate rises\par \par \uc2 * Euro/Dollar short position hits record high\par \par \uc2 (Adds comment, updates prices, byline)\par \par \uc2 By Daniel Bases and Wanfeng Zhou\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, June 1 (Reuters) - The dollar fell against the euro and yen on Friday after a gloomy U.S. jobs report fueled talk the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  may need to take further monetary easing measures to prop up the fragile economy.\par \par \uc2 The euro rebounded off a 23-month low against the dollar as traders scrambled to cover bets against the euro zone common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after driving it down 7 percent in May.\par \par \uc2 Sharp losses for the greenback ensued after Washington reported U.S. employers created a paltry 69,000 jobs last month. It was the fewest since May last year, and the unemployment rate rose for the first time since June. The data added to a slew of recent weak numbers suggesting the economic recovery was faltering.\par \par \uc2 "The 'green shoots' that were providing confidence in the U.S. economy are being mowed over as quickly as they appear," said Douglas Borthwick, managing director of Faros Trading in Stamford, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 "The nonfarm payrolls number gives considerable political capital for the U.S. Federal Reserve to announce further (quantitative easing)," he added. "As the U.S. is reaching peaks for the year, further QE could see this position under extreme stress."\par \par \uc2 The euro waxed and waned as the day progressed only to revisit session highs heading into the close of trade.\par \par \uc2 "There are a lot of shorts out there and I think given the magnitude of the move and the volatility of the jump off the lows this morning just under $1.23, we might see some squaring up into the weekend," said Robert Sinche, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at RBS in Stamford Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 Short positions, or bets against the euro taken by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators in the options market, hit a record high in the latest week, according to data compiled by the Commodities Futures Trading Commission and Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "If there was some aggressive policy announcement over the weekend, people tend to buy back what they have been short and certainly there have been a lot of euro shorts out there," he said.\par \par \uc2 While potential remedies for Europe's credit crisis might be proposed over the calm of the weekend, investors will navigate monetary policy decisions from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank of England, \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  and testimony from U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke before the U.S. Congress.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 0.27 percent to 78.14 yen, after hitting as low as 77.65 on Reuters data, the weakest since mid-February.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in New York trading, the dollar jumped to 78.27 yen\par \par \uc2 from a session low with traders citing market rumors of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities to weaken the yen.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment. RBS's Sinche and \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy Marc Chandler both cited talk in the market of Japan checking rates but said there was no evidence of actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Analysts at Action Economics said there was market speculation the Fed checked rates on the BOJ's behalf.\par \par \uc2 "It just shows how much nervousness is out there right now," Chandler said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up warnings that it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the safe-haven yen's recent climb, saying the rise was being driven by speculators and that it would act decisively if excessive market moves continued.\par \par \uc2 A separate report on U.S. factory activity in May showed some slowing but suggested the economy was not falling off a cliff.\par \par \uc2 COORDINATED ACTION?\par \par \uc2 The euro traded up 0.40 percent to $1.2406, rebounding from a session low of $1.2286, the weakest since July 1, 2010. It had climbed as high as $1.2456 on Reuters data, helped by market talk of coordinated monetary easing by the G20 over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 "If there is a joint (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move Sunday night, I don't think it is end game for the crisis - checkmate on preventing a euro unravelling," said David Gilmore, a partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Connecticut. "It will be an opportunity for many people still long risk to exit at less worse levels."\par \par \uc2 Market speculation is growing the ECB will cut rates from their record low of 1 percent but a Reuters poll showed economists expected it to hold its fire.\par \par \uc2 The euro zone common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also hit its weakest since December 2000 of 95.57 yen, before recouping losses to trade at 96.90 yen, up slightly on the day.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Spain data on Friday showed Spaniards sent money abroad in droves, worried about the health of the country's banks. A net 66.2 billion euros ($82.0 billion) was sent abroad in March, the most since records began in 1990.\par \par \uc2 "It is looking very bearish for the euro with the latest capital flows data showing a significant amount leaving Spanish banks, all of which indicate they will probably need official help," said Peter Kinsella, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Nick Olivari, Steven C. Johnson, Julie Haviv and Richard Leong; Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 8) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | AUF | CANT | J | RBN | ABX | BNX | FUN | UKI | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120531e85v0000z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
