\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  steps up  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  warnings as yen climbs\b0\par\par\uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2012\par 01:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Ready to respond "immediately" vs volatile moves -Nakao\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  tsar also says shouldn't rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Finmin says current yen rise doesn't reflect fundamentals\par \par \uc2 (Adds top financial diplomat, analyst quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara and Rie Ishiguro\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday stepped up warnings that it could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if excessive yen rises continue, with the country's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat threatening action even if U.S. and European partners were not on board.\par \par \uc2 Takehiko Nakao, vice finance minister for international affairs, said it was becoming more obvious that current yen rises were being driven by speculators and warned that Tokyo was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  should such moves continue.\par \par \uc2 "Although there might be differences (in views with the United States and European countries) from time to time, the Japanese government is determined to take an immediate response to volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he told a Euromoney forum.\par \par \uc2 "Monetary policy is important, but we shouldn't exclude the possibility of taking our response in the market, which is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 Nakao's remarks were the most direct warning of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 b y Japanese policymaker since the yen began to creep up again on safe-haven demand amid worries about Europe's deepening debt crisis, and came on the heels of similar comments by Finance Minister Jun Azumi earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 "It is clear that the current one-sided \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves do not reflect the economy's fundamentals," Azumi told a news conference after a cabinet meeting.\par \par \uc2 "We will need to take decisive action if excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves continue."\par \par \uc2 The warnings came as the yen climbed to another 3-1/2 month high against the dollar of 78.21 overnight and an 11-1/2-year high against the euro of 96.48 on the escalating euro zone debt crisis and weak U.S. economic data.\par \par \uc2 Japanese policymakers have used the phrase "decisive action" in the run-up to previous market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it is rare for them to directly mention the word "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " when warning of action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The warnings caught traders' attention though Tohru Sasaki, head of Japan rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at JPMorgan Chase Bank in Tokyo, thought it seemed too early for the authorities to pull the trigger.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think authorities will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this stage. Dollar/yen volatility is low compared with the euro/dollar. Both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are gaining against the euro so \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not win understanding from the United States, which criticised \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year given low volatility in the dollar/yen," he said.\par \par \uc2 "If volatility accelerated and pushed the dollar towards its record low of 75.31 yen in a short span of time, say next week, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would depend on volatility, not levels."\par \par \uc2 BOJ UNDER PRESSURE AGAIN\par \par \uc2 Tokyo spent a record 8 trillion yen ($101 billion) in unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last Oct. 31, when the dollar hit its record low against the yen, and another 1 trillion yen in early November on undeclared forays into the market. Authorities have stayed out of the market since then.\par \par \uc2 The government is keen to shield Japan's export-reliant economy from adverse effects of the strong yen at a time when it faces difficult negotiations with opposition parties on a planned hike in the sales tax.\par \par \uc2 The yen's rise will put the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  under pressure to ease monetary policy further when its policy board meets this month, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would prefer to stand pat for now after having acted in February and April via increases in asset purchases.\par \par \uc2 Japanese exporters won a rare reprieve after the February easing which coincided with signs of improving health of the global economy and drove the yen to 11-month lows against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 But since April the yen has resumed creeping upwards on more euro zone turmoil due to fears that Greece's may leave the euro and more recently that Spain will require a bailout, as well as concerns that the global economic recovery is running out of steam.\par \par \uc2 Many in the BOJ feel little need for further action and want to save their limited policy options for later unless Europe's deepening debt crisis triggers a yen spike to new records and derails Japan's recovery prospects.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Leika Kihara; Editing by Tomasz Janowski and Edwina Gibbs)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/AZUMI  (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | J | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | U | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120601e85v0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
