\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Losses Steam Ahead Of Heavy-Hitting US Data\b0\par\par\uc2 772 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2012\par 13:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Dollar retraces some of the week's gains amid month-end rebalancing\par \par \uc2 -- Euro, Australian dollar, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  pare losses\par \par \uc2 -- Weaker inflation gives ECB room to maneuver to boost economy if required\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Eva Szalay \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON -(Dow Jones)- The dollar retraced some of its sharp recent gains in European trading Thursday as month-end position squaring by dealers lent the euro and higher-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the Australian dollar some support before the publication of heavy-hitting U.S. economic data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In keeping with the modestly calmer tone after a week of building euro-zone anxiety, yields on peripheral euro-zone bonds were flat and those on relatively safer German bunds ticked higher, while shares rose.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The risk-off move which started in London [Wednesday] continued in North America, wrapped up in Asia and since then we have been drifting higher," said Elsa Lignos, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at the Royal Bank of Canada Capital Markets in a note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data which showed the euro-zone's inflation rate slowing to 2.4% on the year in May from 2.6% in April was largely shunned by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets but could nonetheless give the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more wiggle room to cut interest rates ahead of its policy meeting next Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  still struggled against the Japanese yen and remained within sight of its lowest levels since 2000. The dollar also traded below Y79, drawing attention to the possibility of a response from the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which hasn't had to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to fight yen strength since November.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  fired another warning shot to investors, with the bank's vice president Jean-Pierre Danthine aggressively underscoring the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's willingness to defend the CHF1.20 floor in the euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In response, the euro sneaked higher against the Swiss franc but remains within touching distance of the SNB's floor.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors will now be eyeing the U.S. ADP employment report at 1215 GMT and the second estimate of first-quarter U.S. economic growth data at 1230 GMT, ahead of the highly influential U.S. nonfarm payrolls report on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Concerns about a further round of quantitative easing [in the U.S.] are likely to have eased sufficiently to ensure that the ADP report would only affect the dollar exchange rates in case of a very negative surprise," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a research note. "And even then the majority of market participants are likely to wait for the real thing, the official labor market report due on Friday."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also pared some of this week's losses, while the Norwegian krone powered to its highest level against the euro since March after retail sales data proved less negative than in some in the market had expected.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1036 GMT the euro was trading at $1.2411 compared with $1.2367 in New York late Wednesday, according to EBS via CQG. It was trading at Y97.69 from Y97.78 and at CHF1.2015 from CHF1.2009.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pound was at $1.5501 compared with $1.5484 and the Australian dollar was at $0.9739 from CHF0.9706.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was at Y78.79 from Y79.085.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at about 82.871 from 83.082.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A summary of key levels for chart-watching technical strategists is below:\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1025 GMT     1.2410     78.81      1.5514     0.9681 \par 3 Day Trend       Bearish    Bearish    Bearish    Bullish \par Weekly Trend      Bearish    Bearish    Bearish    Bullish \par 200 day ma        1.3275     79.71      1.5868     0.9145 \par 3rd Resistance    1.2495     79.33      1.5612     0.9776 \par 2nd Resistance    1.2456     79.13      1.5548     0.9738 \par 1st Resistance    1.2428     78.81      1.5526     0.9720 \par Pivot*            1.2411     79.16      1.5532     0.9678 \par 1st Support       1.2358     78.70      1.5464     0.9666 \par 2nd Support       1.2295     78.25      1.5408     0.9640 \par 3rd Support       1.2151     78.00      1.5365     0.9595 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       AUD/USD \par  \par Spot 1025 GMT     0.9747 \par 3 Day Trend       Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.0296 \par 3rd Resistance    0.9899 \par 2nd Resistance    0.9857 \par 1st Resistance    0.9800 \par Pivot*            0.9755 \par 1st Support       0.9673 \par 2nd Support       0.9663 \par 3rd Support       0.9614 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By E