\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Yen Climbs Higher As Risk Aversion Deepens\b0\par\par\uc2 836 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2012\par 07:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Euro and dollar fall to fresh multi-month lows against the yen\par \par \uc2 -- Euro could fall further if German data out later comes out weaker than expected\par \par \uc2 -- Japan's finance minister Azumi warns on yen's strength\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Alexander Martin \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar and euro fell to fresh multi-month lows against the yen during Asian trading Thursday as investors flocked to the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid a barrage of negative news from the euro zone, and analysts said the yen-buying is likely to increase.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar breached its previous day low of Y78.86, its lowest level since Feb. 17, while the euro fell below key support at Y97.50 and neared its Jan. 16 low of Y97.04.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market participants flocked to the yen, seen as a safe-haven investment, as growing concerns about Spain's banking problems sent Spanish and Italian bond yields higher.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on Spanish 10-year debt spiked as high as 6.65%, near levels that drove Greece, Portugal and Ireland to bailouts, as Spain's EFE news agency reported that the Spanish government would fund beleaguered Bankia's EUR19 billion rescue by selling treasury bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy's 10-year yield also climbed 15 bps to 6.02%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks sank in Europe and the U.S., while Asian markets also opened lower, with Japan's Nikkei Stock Index down 1.8% at midday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "As the European situation is growing increasingly severe, it's likely that yen-buying pressure will increase," said Sumino Kamei, senior analyst at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\f28 \uc2 \f2  UFJ.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Uchida Minori, chief analyst at BTMU, said that, with dollar long-positions piling up before major indicators such as U.S. non-farm payrolls and the ISM manufacturing report, participants may be adjusting their positions, temporarily weakening the dollar against the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said yen-crosses were being sold, and the market was flow-driven at month-end. The 200-day moving average technical support for the dollar was at around Y76.60, with stop loss orders seen near Y76.50, they said, which if breached could send the dollar lower against the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of 0450 GMT, the dollar was at Y78.75 from Y79.05 late Wednesday in New York, according to trading platform EBS. The euro was at $1.2387 from $1.2367 and at Y97.55 from Y97.78.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister ratcheted up his warnings against the rising yen Thursday, but stopped short of hinting at any immediate direct market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This is not reflecting the state of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economy," Jun Azumi said when asked about the yen's strength. "It is a little speculative."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, traders say repeated warnings from Azumi suggest that authorities are increasingly concerned about the yen's impact on the economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I wouldn't be surprised," if the MOF conducts another round of yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the current level, one dealer said, though he added that "the chance is still low."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looking ahead, the euro could weaken further if German retail sales and unemployment data scheduled for release later in the day come out worse than expected, said Junichi Ishikawa, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at IG Market Securities in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "And with the European debt crisis assuming serious proportions, attention will center on moves by the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Expectations of an ECB rate-cut may be heightened, he said, adding that a third round of the ECB's long-term refinancing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , aimed at bolstering the region's banks, could be on the horizon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That could further increase euro-selling pressure, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 82.938 from about 83.082.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                                     2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par Dollar Rates \par USD/JPY Japan            78.74-78       79.05-09  -0.39    79.13    78.72  +2.40 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.2387-88      1.2365-68  +0.17   1.2387   1.2358  -4.42 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.5480-82      1.5477-81  +0.01   1.5484   1.5464  -0.39 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.9696-98      0.9709-13  -0.15   0.9719   0.9698  +3.46 \par USD/CAD Canada          1.0291-92     1.0298-303  -0.09   1.0312   1.0292  +0.80 \par AUD/USD Australia       0.9710-14      0.9703-07  +0.07   0.9719   0.9674  -4.86 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.7535-40      0.7529-34  +0.08   0.7538   0.7502  -3.07 \par  \par Euro Rates \par  \par EUR/JPY Japan            97.54-58       97.76-81  -0.23    97.90    97.36  -2.01 \par  \par Source: \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICAP Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 