\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW: Euro May Lose Another 10% Against Dlr, Yen -  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Concepts Asia Head\b0\par\par\uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2012\par 06:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Asia head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Concepts, one of world's largest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedge funds, says fund bearish on euro due to European debt problems\par \par \uc2 -- Says dollar, yen the "two winning horses" this year\par \par \uc2 -- Though ineffective, fund expects more BOJ easing, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The euro is likely to lose another 10% against the dollar and yen by the year-end as the European debt problem is worsening and its outlook remains highly unclear, says the Asia head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedge fund \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Concepts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are very bearish on the euro. Nobody can tell what will happen to Greece and the euro in the next 12 months," Bernard Lock, director and regional manager of the fund told Dow Jones Newswires in an interview.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lock expects the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely fall to $1.22 and Y96 by the end of June and $1.10 and Y90 by the end of December. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Concepts, one of world's largest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedge funds, has $4 billion in assets under management. Earlier on Wednesday, it fell to $1.2457, its lowest level since July 2010 and to Y98.95, nearing its Jan. 23 low of Y98.94.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The likelihood of Athens exiting from the euro zone isn't high yet, he said, because the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and other euro-zone members will try their best to keep the troubled nation inside the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But he added that it all depends on Greece's June 17 election, pointing out that many investors are being forced to hedge against the risk of a euro exit, by selling the unit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 No matter what the outcome of the current stage of the crisis, though, worries over Greece aren't likely to disappear for years to come, Lock said. The nation's competitiveness is very low due to its economic structure, he said, adding that the government could easily find itself struggling again with repeated large deficits.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Even if all the outstanding debts are written off, it doesn't solve the problem because the deficit will come back in another five or 10 years," Lock said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The fund also sees the Australian dollar weakening due to the slowdown of China's economy. Lock expects the Australian unit will reach US$0.88 by the end of the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said he is putting his biggest bets on the dollar and yen this year, describing them as "the top two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When it comes to the dollar against the yen, Lock expects the dollar to weaken against the yen toward summer as the problems in Europe are likely to worsen further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 From the end of the year, though, the dollar should start rising at a gradual pace, ending this year's trade around Y83, he said, since the dollar index's multiyear trend over past decades suggests the greenback will enter a rising trend over the next five years and beyond.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The dollar has a good chance of touching Y77.00 this summer, and if that level cannot be held, it will go to Y75," Lock said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New York-based fund expects the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  will take more easing measures in the months to come and the finance ministry will conduct solo yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should the dollar rapidly drop below Y78.00 or if it falls to its record-low of Y75.31.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But any efforts by Japan won't be able to stave off the flow of an entire market seeking a safe haven, Lock said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Japan will be a lone warrior," and its fight "will be ineffective," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 30-05-12 0437GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120530e85u0007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
