\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 3-BOJ holds off on easing; eyes on Europe risks\b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2012\par 05:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 23 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  kept monetary policy steady on Wednesday, preferring to save its ammunition as Europe's deepening debt crisis could warrant action in coming months to fend off damage to the fragile economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained its view that Japan's economy will resume a moderate recovery, but warned that it needs to carefully watch market moves for now because they are jittery due to worries about Europe's sovereign debt problems.\par \par \uc2 ***********************************************************\par \par \uc2 KEY POINTS:\par \par \uc2 -- As widely expected, the BOJ maintained its key policy rate at a range of zero to 0.1 percent by a unanimous vote.\par \par \uc2 -- Governor \uc2 Masaaki Shirakawa\uc2  will hold an embargoed news conference with his comments expected to come out sometime after 4:15 p.m. (0715 GMT).\par \par \uc2 COMMENTARY:\par \par \uc2 YASUHIDE YAJIMA, CHIEF ECONOMIST, NLI RESEARCH INSTITUTE, TOKYO\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ stood pat as expected but it is likely to ease next in July, based on recent patterns. It could bring forward the timing depending on Europe's debt problems and how that affects the yen.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely finding it more difficult than before to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market given international pressure, so if the yen spikes to around 77 to the dollar, the BOJ may act first through monetary policy to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ is expected to extend the duration of government bonds it buys to five years in the future, to smooth out its bond-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Before doing so, it could tweak its banknote rule that limits its JGB holdings in the first half of this year."\par \par \uc2 YOSHIMASA MARUYAMA, CHIEF ECONOMIST, ITOCHU ECONOMIC RESEARCH INSTITUTE, TOKYO\par \par \uc2 "Solid GDP in January-March showed the economy was recovering with support from reconstruction being felt, and although today's trade data lacked strength, the direction of the economic recovery is in line with the BOJ's view.\par \par \uc2 "I think there is little chance that the BOJ would ease policy further in July (when it reviews its long-term growth forecasts) as some anticipate, as long as the economic recovery remains on track as the BOJ expects.\par \par \uc2 "That said, if Europe's turmoil intensifies and impacts financial markets, then the BOJ may have to take action in response to market moves."\par \par \uc2 KATSUTOSHI INADOME, BOND STRATEGIST, MITSUBISHI UFJ MORGAN STANLEY SECURITIES\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ may be hoping that political pressure on the bank to do more will fade away now that it has eased in February and April. But I expect the pressure to continue, and that could force the bank to ease policy again in July when its price projections will likely show it has a long way to go before achieving its inflation goal of 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 "Further easing might come as early as next month depending on financial market moves ahead of the FOMC meeting and Greece's second election. If the BOJ were to ease further, it would likely boost its asset-purchase scheme.\par \par \uc2 "With the BOJ failing to meet its JGB purchase targets in recent \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , financial markets will scrutinise what the BOJ governor may say about how it will deal with the financial market environment."\par \par \uc2 MARKET REACTION:\par \par \uc2 - For yen updates click ; for prices click\par \par \uc2 - For JGB updates, click, for prices click\par \par \uc2 - For stocks click, for the Nikkei share average click\par \par \uc2 LINKS:\par \par \uc2 For BOJ website click: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.boj.or.jp/en/index.htm/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.boj.or.jp/en/index.htm/}}}\par \par \uc2 BACKGROUND:\par \par \uc2 - Japan's economy bounced back in the first quarter from a year-end lull, powering ahead of other major industrial nations thanks to rebuilding of the tsunami-battered northeast, solid consumer spending and improvement in exports.\par \par \uc2 - The BOJ eased policy by boosting asset purchases in February and April in a largely symbolic move to show its determination to achieve its 1 percent inflation target.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Leika Kihara, Rie Ishiguro and Kaori Kaneko; Editing by Chris Gallagher)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/BOJ (INSTANT VIEW 3) | J | ABN | E | RBN | M | D | U | NAT | UKI   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120526e85n0000w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
