\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2012\par 12:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH DOWNGRADES JAPAN TO 'A+', OUTLOOK NEGATIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings on Tuesday downgraded Japan's sovereign rating to A+ and said that it was maintaining a negative outlook as Japan struggles with reining in its dire fiscal balance. (published 1018 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD SEES US GROWING MORE THAN 2% IN 2012 AND 2013 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (\f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES\f28 \uc2 \f2 )--The U.S. economy is likely to grow above its potential through 2013, drawing down the unemployment rate to 7.4%, according to new forecasts by the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD SEES EURO-ZONE GDP -0.1% IN 2012; +0.9% IN 2013 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PARIS (Dow Jones)--The Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development Tuesday slashed its forecasts for growth across the euro zone for this year and next, and warned that the area's debt crisis could pull it into a vicious downward spiral without the right policy action.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREEK BANKS TO GET EUR18B RECAPITALIZATION DOWNPAYMENT FRI-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Greece's banks will get their much-delayed lifeline Friday, a senior official with one of the country's largest banks told Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EFSF'S STRAUCH: GREECE MUST HONOR COMMITMENTS OR LOSE FUNDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Greece must honor its commitments to its international creditors or risk being cut off from Europe's bailout fund, a top official said Tuesday. (published 1035 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF LAGARDE: EXPECT GREEK GOVT TO IMPLEMENT BAILOUT PROGRAM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects Greece's next government to implement its agreed bailout program, IMF managing director \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christine Lagarde\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 1041 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  SPANISH, DUTCH FUNDING COSTS MOVE OPPOSITE AT AUCTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spain's borrowing costs rose further at Tuesday's Treasury bill auction, underlying the market's unease with the country's funding sustainability as bank recapitalization needs, frail finances in some of its regions and an upwardly revised 2011 fiscal deficit put pressure on the budget. (published 1028 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAUDI FIN MIN: NO PLANS TO CHANGE SPENDING IF OIL PRICES FALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Falling crude oil prices won't derail the massive social spending program currently underway in Saudi Arabia, the kingdom's finance minister said Tuesday. (published 1018 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF SAYS UK SHOULD EASE AUSTERITY DRIVE IF ECONOMY WEAKENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. Finance Minister George Osborne should slow the pace of his austerity drive if economic growth fails to pick up soon, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 1000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD SAYS UK ECONOMY TO RETURN TO GROWTH IN SECOND HALF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The U.K. economy will likely return to growth in the second half of the year with recovery threatened by a possible global slowdown, the Organisation for Economic Co-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Development said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD: CHINA GDP GROWTH LIKELY TO REBOUND ON STIMULUS EFFORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--China's economic growth is likely to rebound some time this year due to government stimulus policies and a restocking of inventories, the Organization of Economic Cooperation and Development said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S ECON TO GROW ABOUT 2% IN 2012 ON RECONSTRUCTION SPENDING, EXPAND 1.5% IN 2013 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said Tuesday that Japan's disaster-hit economy will rebound to solid growth this year, led by reconstruction spending, and keep expanding at a slower pace in 2013.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: JBIC WATANABE SAYS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NOT HINDERED BY US STANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials should not feel "tied down" by U.S. opposition to direct market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as every sovereign nation retains the right to act against sharp moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates, a former top Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Tuesday. (published 1040 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD: EMERGING EUROPE WOULD GAIN FROM EASING OF EURO-ZONE TENSIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--An easing of tensions in the euro zone would help boost growth in a number of eastern European and other economies with close trade and financial ties to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area next year, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER REPEATS CALLS FOR PROPER BOJ ACTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister reiterated Tuesday that he wants the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  to act appropriately at the right time, ahead of the start of a two-day policy meeting by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later in the day. (published 0038 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN REMAINS WORLD'S LARGEST CREDITOR NATION IN 2011 - MOF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan retained its title as the world's biggest creditor nation in 2011, as the government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and firms' overseas mergers and acquisitions helped boost the value of the country's foreign investment holdings. (published 2341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK APR ANNUAL CPI SLOWDOWN SHARPER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. annual consumer price inflation slowed more sharply than expected in April and meant Bank of England Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mervyn King\f28 \uc2 \f2  did not have to write a letter explaining the high level of inflation to Chancellor of the Exchequer George Osborne, data showed Tuesday. (published 0941 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK PUBLIC SECTOR POSTS RECORD NET REPAYMENT IN APRIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. posted a record public sector net repayment in April due mainly to a one-off boost from the transfer of the pension assets of the state-owned mail company to the public coffers, official data showed Tuesday. (published 0943 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD SLASHES AUSTRALIA 2012 GDP FORECAST TO 3% FROM 4% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Paris-based Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development Tuesday slashed its forecast for Australian economic growth, warning of a tough year ahead with pain from widening performance gaps between industries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOE'S MILES: STIMULUS HELPED AVERT DEEPER DOWNTURN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Monetary policy can't solve all the U.K.'s economic problems but quantitative easing has helped avert a deeper downturn, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  policy maker David Miles said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par POLISH \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  READY TO ACT TO CURB ZLOTY VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to counteract excessive zloty volatility and speculation on the market, but does not target any specific level it plans to defend, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  executive management board member Andrzej Raczko told TVN CNBC Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRIA FIN MIN: HOLLANDE'S DEBT CRISIS APPROACH "NONSENSE" -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--French President Francois Hollande's approach to solving the euro-zone debt crisis is "nonsense," Austria's Finance Minister Maria Fekter said in an interview published Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : 0.3% ON-YEAR 1Q GDP GROWTH BETTER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--Thailand's 0.3% on-year growth in first-quarter gross domestic product was better than the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 's projected contraction of 0.17%, the director of the bank's Macroeconomic Policy and Analysis Office, Songtum Pinto, said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAUDI ECONOMY WILL CONTINUE TO SEE STRONG GROWTH THIS YEAR -FIN MIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RIYADH (Zawya Dow Jones)--Saudi Arabia will continue to experience strong growth this year, even as the risks to the global economy remain high and its recovery gradual, the kingdom's minister of finance said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -BACKED PAPER ARGUES FOR CAPITAL-ACCOUNT OPENING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A front-page article in the Financial News, a newspaper backed by China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , argued on Tuesday that conditions are currently ripe to open up the country's capital account, citing a number of government officials and scholars. (published 0156 GMT) [ 22-05-12 1003GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120522e85m000m5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
