\par\par \b \uc2 DJ WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 :Yen Rallies To Three-Month High Vs Dollar-2-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anusha Shrivastava   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2012\par 00:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The yen shot to a three-month high against the dollar, in its biggest single-day jump in over a year, after a weak reading of mid-Atlantic manufacturing cast new doubt on the health of the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia\uc2 's manufacturing index fell to -5.8 for May, well below economists' average forecast of 9.3. Anything below 0 indicates contraction in Philadelphia-area business activity.\par \par \uc2 Negative indicators play into expectations that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will have to resume buying bonds in order to prop up the economy. This practice, known as easing, increases the amount of dollars in circulation, weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies have an outsized impact on the dollar-yen exchange rate. Since interest rates are near zero in both the U.S. and Japan, investors tend to shift their money when the Fed or \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  makes a move that puts pressure on the dollar or yen. \uc2 The Fed\uc2 's policy board meets next month, while the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  is not expected to introduce more easing measures at its meeting next week.\par \par \uc2 "The yen is going to be the most sensitive to U.S. data," said Mark McCormick, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday in New York, the yen was trading at 79.26 to the dollar. That was just off its intraday peak of 79.13, its strongest exchange rate since Feb. 17. The move higher was the biggest in absolute and percentage terms since March 2011. On Wednesday, the dollar was at Y80.33. The dollar was at CHF0.9459 on Thursday from CHF0.9445.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese government could put a cap on the yen rally, however. \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said repeatedly that they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market if the yen gets too strong. They last stepped in when the yen neared 75 to the dollar in October, but the bar could be higher now, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "I think there is a high possibility to see [\uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... if yen dips below 79, considering the fact how serious Japanese authorities are to tackle yen strength," said Masafumi Takada, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The euro also gained after the Philadelphia Fed data, but ended the New York trading day at $1.2697 from $1.2716 on Wednesday. It slipped when Alexis Tsipras, the head of Greece's radical left Syriza party, said Greece could stop debt payments if Europe cuts off funding, though he added that his country should stay part of the euro. Greece is scheduled to hold a second election on June 17, after parties failed to form a government following a poll earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 A potential Greek exit from the euro has sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spiraling lower, dropping in 13 of the last 14 trading days.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 81.474 from about 81.372.\par \par \uc2 The U.K. pound was at $1.5798 from $1.5909.\par \par \uc2 -By Anusha Shrivastava, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2227; anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020120517e85h00ayh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
