\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar bounces back after U.S. manufacturing surprise\b0\par\par\uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2012\par 01:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * US ISM data shows strongest growth in 10 months\par \par \uc2 * Dollar/yen back above Y80, off 2-1/2-month lows\par \par \uc2 * With dlr/yen at chart crossroads, Friday's U.S. jobs data seen key\par \par \uc2 * Euro looks to ECB, weekend elections\par \par \uc2 By Hideyuki Sano\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 2 (Reuters) - The dollar bounced back on Wednesday from 2-1/2-month lows against the Japanese yen after upbeat U.S. manufacturing data soothed fears the economy was slowing, though gains were kept minimal ahead of key events such as the U.S. jobs data.\par \par \uc2 The Institute of Supply Management (ISM) report showed the strongest rate of U.S. factory growth in 10 months, a surprise after a string of disappointing U.S. data and countering recent speculation the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will embark on a third round of bond buying to bolster the economy.\par \par \uc2 "After the surprisingly strong ISM number, the next job data will be more important than usual. If it is strong, it could cement expectation of strong recovery at least in the United States," said Mitsuru Saito, chief economist at \uc2 Tokai Tokyo Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The payroll data is due on Friday, with economists looking to a job increase of around 170,000 in April, after a disappointing gain of 120,000 in March.\par \par \uc2 "If the job data sparks risk-on mood, that should lead to the yen's fall and rise in bond yields. This weekend has a chance of triggering such a trend," he added.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rebounded above 80.00 yen and last stood at 80.110. Its recovery from a trough of 79.640 yen hit on Tuesday caught speculators short and forced them to buy back the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The market is showing a straightforward reaction to the ISM numbers. But with the payroll data looming ahead, you can't expect the dollar to keep rising," said Sumino Kamei, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at the \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ.\par \par \uc2 Chartists say if the payroll data helps the dollar to end the week above 80.42, the cloud top on weekly Ichimoku charts, that could indicate its fall below that major chart level was a false alarm, putting the dollar on course for a further recovery.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if it falls below 79.55-60 area, its high after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Oct. 31 dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the 100-day moving average, that in turn could fan bearish mood on the dollar.\par \par \uc2 HIT BY AUSTERITY\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, a measure of the dollar against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also stood off a two-month trough of 78.603 hit on Tuesday. It last stood at 78.883, almost flat on the day.\par \par \uc2 The euro retreated slightly to $1.3211 as traders tried to hunt for stop-loss orders, slipping from a one-month peak of $1.3284 hit overnight.\par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been stuck around $1.3235/45 for four trading days with dealers citing talk of central banks on both sides of the market to hem in price action.\par \par \uc2 The euro's fortune is seen largely hinging on Thursday's European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting and weekend elections in Greece and France, on top of Friday's U.S. job report.\par \par \uc2 While few market players expect any major policy changes from the ECB, some market players see dovish comments from its chief Mario Draghi as austerity-hit countries such as Spain are slipping into recession.\par \par \uc2 The two elections on Sunday -- one for French President and the other for Greek parliament -- keep many market players on guard.\par \par \uc2 Francois Hollande, front-runner and first-round winner in the French race, has promised to shift the debate in Europe towards promoting growth if he is elected, which leads some market players to worry about potential tension between Berlin and Paris.\par \par \uc2 But others have played down such fears, noting that Germany appears to be relaxing its focus on austerity.\par \par \uc2 Potentially more unpredictable is the election in Greece, where the two main pro-bailout parties are thought to have only a wafer-thin lead to form a coalition government over smaller anti-bailout parties.\par \par \uc2 A failure to win a majority by the two parties that support the bailout scheme by the international lenders would open a can of worms for policymakers and send the euro reeling, market players said.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar was nursing heavy losses after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 's surprisingly large 50 basis-point rate cut on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 It showed limited reaction to a slight upgrade in \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's China PMI and last traded at $1.0336 after suffering a near 1 percent fall on Tuesday, the biggest one-day decline in six weeks.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Cecile Lefort in Sydney; Editing by Muralikumar Anantharaman)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | AUF | ABN | D | E | RBN | J | M | NAT | ND | SI | U | UKI | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120501e85100135\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
