\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For April 2\b0\par\par\uc2 1,713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2012\par 09:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: BOJ TANKAN SHOWS BIG MFRS STILL CAUTIOUS, ADDS TO EASING EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's closely watched tankan corporate survey showed Monday that the yen's recent fall from historic highs and a recovery of supply chains failed to cheer business sentiment, likely adding to expectations for more easing by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: SINGAPORE PRIVATE HOME PRICES FALL FOR 1ST TIME SINCE 2Q 09 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Private home prices in Singapore fell in the first quarter from the previous three-month period, snapping two-and-a-half years of growth as a slowing economy and recent government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crimped real estate investments. (published 0552 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINESE VICE PREMIER VOICES CONFIDENCE ABOUT LOCAL ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Vice Premier Li Keqiang said Monday that the country has the ability to maintain solid growth over the long run, in a bid to boost confidence in the world's second-largest economy which is facing a slowdown. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN AUTO SALES SURGE IN MARCH AS SUBSIDIES IGNITE DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sales of new cars, trucks and buses in Japan jumped 78.2% in March from a year earlier, gaining for the seventh-straight month as government subsidies for fuel-efficient cars continued to drive demand. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WEAK AUSTRALIA HOUSING DEMAND TO DRAG ON ECONOMIC GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian building approvals were much weaker than expected in February sending a clear signal that interest rate cuts in late 2011 have failed to spur demand with housing set to drag on economic growth in the first quarter. (published 0255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA INFLATION EASES TO 20-MONTH LOW IN MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's consumer inflation unexpectedly eased for a third straight month to a 20-month low in March, adding to official data that suggest the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will have more flexibility on monetary policy this year. (published 0318 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDONESIA INFLATION ACCELERATES IN MARCH, PRESSURE TO REMAIN HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's inflation accelerated in March due to higher prices for spices and increased buying of daily necessities ahead of a proposed rise in subsidized fuel prices. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDIA FEBRUARY TRADE DEFICIT $15.2 BLN VS $9.3 BLN YEAR AGO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's trade deficit in February widened to $15.2 billion from $9.3 billion a year earlier as weakening demand hurt export growth. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FORMER PBOC ADVISER: ECONOMY WILL LIKELY GROW 8.3%-8.5% THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The continued moderation of China's economy reflects a "soft landing" process, and gross domestic product will probably grow 8.3% to 8.5% this year, a former adviser to the People's Bank of China said Monday. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SHOULD STRENGHTHEN TWO-WAY YUAN FLEXIBILITY - PAPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should strengthen efforts to expand two-way flexibility of the yuan, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -backed newspaper said in a commentary Monday. (published 0642 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ YAMAGUCHI: BOJ PROVIDING AMPLE YEN FUNDS INTO MKT WHILE LEAVING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUNDS UNSTERILIZED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deputy Gov. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hirohide Yamaguchi\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has injected ample funds into the banking system, while leaving the funds obtained from yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unsterilized. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  MARCH MANUFACTURING PMI FALLS TO 54.7 FROM 56.6 IN FEB - MARKIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's manufacturing activity slowed for the second straight month in March, but business conditions indicated a marked improvement as local demand picked up. (published 0553 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN INDEX OF COMMODITY PRICES UP 1.9% IN MARCH -RBA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index of Australian commodity prices rose 1.9% in Australian dollar terms in March, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA DEPUTY FINANCE MINISTER: EXPECT MOODY'S TO RAISE SOVEREIGN RATING BY 1 NOTCH WITHIN A YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government expects Moody's Investors Service to raise the country's sovereign credit rating by one notch to Aa3 within a year after the ratings firm upgraded the Asian nation's ratings outlook to positive from stable, Deputy Minister for International Affairs at the Ministry of Strategy and Finance Choi Jong-ku said Monday. (published 0341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: INDONESIA FUEL HIKE DELAY HIGHLIGHTS CONSTRAINTS ON RATING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's backtracking on a planned fuel price hike--aimed at cutting the government's massive fuel-subsidy burden--highlights constraints on the country's sovereign ratings, but is unlikely to weigh heavily on its credit profile, an analyst at Fitch Ratings said Monday. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SINGAPORE'S DBS SEEKS TO BUY INDONESIA'S DANAMON FOR US$7.3 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DBS Group Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., southeast Asia's largest bank by assets, Monday said it plans to acquire Indonesia's PT Bank Danamon for S$9.1 billion as the Singapore group looks to boost its exposure to growing emerging markets in its region. (published 0147 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHALCO TO BUY UP TO 60% OF SOUTHGOBI IN UP TO HK$7.20 BLN DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aluminum Corp. of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ltd., or Chalco, has agreed to buy a controlling stake in Mongolian coal miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 SouthGobi Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . from Canada's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ivanhoe Mines Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . in a deal worth as much as HK$7.20 billion as the Chinese aluminum producer diversifies into the resource-rich country. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN AUTO SALES SURGE IN MARCH AS SUBSIDIES IGNITE DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sales of new cars, trucks and buses in Japan jumped 78.2% in March from a year earlier, gaining for the seventh-straight month as government subsidies for fuel-efficient cars continued to drive demand. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA COURT UPHOLDS $159 MLN AWARD TO SAIL FOR VIOLATION OF CONTRACT BY VALE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An Indian court has upheld an award of $159 million in damages to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Steel Authority of India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to be paid by the Australian unit of miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vale SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  for not fulfilling a coking coal supply contract. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: MITSUBISHI HEAVY SUSPENDS CONSTRUCTION OF US WIND TURBINE FACTORY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has suspended construction of its wind turbine factory in Fort Smith, Arkansas citing weaker-than-expected turbine demand in the U.S. amid rising gas-fired power output. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE GIC ASSET MANAGEMENT HEAD ADDS ROLE AS DEPUTY CHIEF INVESTMENT OFFICER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Government of Singapore Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has appointed the head of its asset management arm, Lim Chow Kiat, to an additional role as deputy group chief investment officer, the sovereign wealth fund said Monday. (published 0409 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA INVESTMENT CORP NAMES LEE DONG-IK AS CHIEF INVESTMENT OFFICER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday named \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lee Dong-ik\f28 \uc2 \f2  the sovereign wealth fund's new chief investment officer. (published 0403 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN FINANCE MINISTER: STOCK-GAINS TAX DECISION IN A MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan Finance Minister Christina Liu said Monday the government will decide in a month if it will tax capital gains from stocks. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PAXYS UNIT SELLS 100% STAKE IN PAXYS AUSTRALIA FOR A$84.9 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Paxys, Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . a Philippine holding firm that focuses on investments in business process outsourcing, said Monday that its unit Paxys N.V. sold its 100% stake in Paxys Australia Pty. Ltd. to SmartGroup Investments Pty. Ltd. for A$84.9 million. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GODREJ PROPERTIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SELL 49% STAKE IN UNIT TO PRIVATE EQUITY FIRM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Godrej Properties Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said it has agreed to sell a 49% stake in a unit to private equity firm ASK Property Investment Advisors. (published 0318 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GOLDMAN SACHS\f28 \uc2 \f2  SAYS KEEN ON TAPPING GROWTH OPPORTUNITIES IN INDIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . remains committed to India and is keen to tap opportunities to grow alongside the local economy and its capital markets, Chairman and Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lloyd C. Blankfein\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HYUNDAI HEAVY\f28 \uc2 \f2  SETS UP $200 MLN CAR BATTERIES JV WITH MAGNA E-CAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Heavy Industries Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's largest shipbuilder by orders, said Monday it has set up a $200 million joint venture with Magna E-Car, a Canadian electric-car parts supplier, to develop batteries for electric vehicles. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YANG MING MARINE SWINGS TO NET LOSS IN 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yang Ming Marine Transport Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday posted a net loss of NT$9.40 billion for 2011, compared to a net profit of NT$11.79 billion in 2010. (published 0602 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; CHINA PMI SUPPORTS, WEAKER YEN LIFTS TOKYO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most Asian stock markets were modestly higher Monday, starting off a new quarter on a cautiously optimistic view over the global growth outlook following upbeat data in China and the U.S., while a weaker yen lifted Tokyo shares. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA ALLOWS \f28 \uc2 \f2 TITAN INDUSTRIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO IMPORT GOLD DIRECTLY -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India has allowed jewelry maker Titan Industries to import gold directly for domestic sales, dropping the necessity of routing imports of the precious metal through banks or designated state-run agencies. (published 0701 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA OIL MINISTER: SOUGHT MORE OIL, NATURAL GAS FROM QATAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India has sought more crude oil and natural gas from Qatar, Indian Oil Minister Jaipal Reddy said Monday, as the world's second-fastest growing major economy seeks to augment energy supplies. (published 0618 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: MITSUBISHI HEAVY SUSPENDS CONSTRUCTION OF US WIND TURBINE FACTORY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has suspended construction of its wind turbine factory in Fort Smith, Arkansas citing weaker-than-expected turbine demand in the U.S. amid rising gas-fired power output. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BHP, \f28 \uc2 \f2 MITSUBISHI\f28 \uc2 \f2  DECLARE FORCE MAJEURE AT AUSTRALIA COAL MINES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-04-12 0716GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A coal mining alliance between \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has declared force majeure at its coal mines in Queensland's Bowen Basin due to industrial action and wet weather, BHP said Monday. (published 0554 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ONGC, CONOCO SIGN PACT ON SHALE GAS, DEEPWATER EXPLORATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's state-run Oil & Natural Gas signs an initial agreement with \f28 \uc2 \f2 ConocoPhillips\f28 \uc2 \f2  to screen opportunities for jointly exploring and developing shale-gas reserves in India and North America and deep-water blocks along India's east coast. [ 02-04-12 0716GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120402e842000fz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
