\par\par \b \uc2 DJ WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Gains On Dollar As Bernanke Strikes Cautious Tone-2-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Stephen L. Bernard   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 00:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell Monday to its lowest point against the euro since March 1 after Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke questioned whether the improving U.S. jobs market could maintain momentum.\par \par \uc2 The euro climbed as high as $1.3368 during New York trading hours before trading at $1.3358 late, according to EBS via CQG. The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at $1.3271 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 During a speech at the National Association for Business Economics, Ben Bernanke acknowledged the employment market was improving. However, Bernanke cautioned that labor markets were still relatively stagnant, and raised questions about whether the recent dip in the unemployment rate was sustainable.\par \par \uc2 Market participants interpreted Bernanke's latest comments as a renewed sense of caution compared with a perceived more optimistic tone from the Fed following its meeting earlier this month and more upbeat comments from Bernanke in recent statements.\par \par \uc2 Investors parse every comment from Bernanke to try and determine whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will embark on another round of asset purchases known as quantitative easing. To do so would hurt the dollar broadly.\par \par \uc2 "Bernanke's comments were more dovish than markets expected and that's being reflected in the dollar," said Todd McDonald, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading for the Americas at Standard Chartered in New York.\par \par \uc2 The added supply of dollars in the market from potential Fed bond purchases would make the greenback a cheaper option to fund investments in higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and assets.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell against the pound and Swiss franc as well Monday. The pound was at $1.5971 from $1.5869 late Friday. The dollar was at CHF0.9030 from CHF0.9080 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 78.908 from 79.345.\par \par \uc2 Despite the broad retreat, the dollar still managed to post gains against the yen Monday. Analysts said that was largely a carryover from the euro's sharp rally against the yen and not as reflective of any kind of dollar strength.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at Y82.82 from Y82.33 late Friday. The euro climbed to Y110.63 in late Monday trading from Y109.35.\par \par \uc2 The euro is now approaching its highest levels of the past six months against the yen, which could lead it to run into some resistance.\par \par \uc2 Resistance could come from Japanese exporters that would look to lock in the yen at the lower price against the euro than it has traded in recent months, said Yujiro Goto, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research strategist at Nomura Securities in New York. Goto said the euro above Y110 was a "good sell zone" for the cross.\par \par \uc2 The euro traded as high as Y111.43 last week, which was near its six-month high of Y111.57. That came on Oct. 31, the last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 -By Stephen L. Bernard, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-4528; stephen.bernard@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Javier E. David and Anusha Shrivastava contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020120326e83q00b41\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
