\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Euro-Yen Nears Key Upside Levels, 'Sell Zone'\b0\par\par\uc2 1,246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 17:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 11:41 (Dow Jones) The euro is approaching two key levels that should be closely watched, but it is in a "good sell zone," says Nomura. It's back above Y110 Monday and could now be targeting Y111.43, last week's high. Nomura notes the euro could also be moving toward Y111.57, hit on Halloween and the last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The investment bank notes that above Y110, Japanese exporters are likely to sell the euro for yen. (stephen.bernard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:35 (Dow Jones) The American Meat Institute says there would need to be 1.5M more cattle annually to replace lean finely textured beef--better known these days as pink slime. Retailers and restaurant chains, among others, are being rejected amid consumer concerns about the product. There were about 33.5M cattle slaughtered last year, according to the USDA. Troy Vetterkind of Vetterkind Cattle Brokerage predicts lean-beef prices will move higher and cheaper cuts could "begin to fit into grinding formulations" as a result of the pink-slime backlash. Cargill notes options include grinding more beef that was previously not ground, imports or a combination. (curt.thacker@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:32 (Dow Jones) Emerging market economies, the major drivers of commodity demand, are finally starting to feel the brunt of high energy prices. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  notes demand for Chinese fuel products was "anemic" in February, growing just 1.5%, or 148,000 barrels a day. The weak demand comes amid a steep rise in fuel costs. A March 19 increase in diesel and gasoline prices is the largest in two years, firm writes. Nymex crude for May up 0.2% at $107.06/bbl. (dan.strumpf@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:31 (Dow Jones) \uc2 BATS Global Markets\uc2 ' share of US share trading a bit lower than usual in first trading session after its IPO debacle Friday, according to the company's own tabulations of equities market share. BATS' two exchanges today account for 10.5% of all US stock trading, vs month-to-date average of 10.9%, though overall trading volume in US stock markets looks generally lackluster so far. Company's markets in US and Europe opened as per usual Monday. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:24 (Dow Jones) \uc2 KB Home\uc2  (KBH) slides further as investors and Wall Street continue digesting the builder's weak F1Q reports. "As one of the more-leveraged homebuilders with one of the more-rapidly eroding book values, we see KB more dependent than most on the pace, proximity and its participation in housing recovery," says \uc2 Stifel Nicolaus\uc2 . \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  puts it more bluntly: "We view KBH as one of the more-poorly positioned companies currently, given a lagging ability to restore profitability." And while MKM Partners cuts its price target to $10 from $13, RBC remains supportive, saying it still expects KBH to be profitable on an operating basis this year. Shares are down 5% at $9.78, putting this month's drop at 14%. (dawn.wotapka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:23 (Dow Jones) \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2  (HOG) is benefiting from the warm weather, with domestic retail sales up at least in the high\u8208\'20\'10single\u8208\'20\'10digit range so far in 1Q, William Blair says in a report that echoes sentiment expressed by BMO last week. Blair also sees international results showing strength, with HOG's European \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  continuing to be bolstered by stronger results in emerging markets such as Russia and Eastern Europe. HOG has expanded its international business to approximately 36% of retail sales, with nearly 20% stemming from Europe, where HOG now holds the No. 2 market share position behind \uc2 BMW\uc2 , firm says. HOG up 1.6% to $49.86. (karen.talley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:20 (Dow Jones) Results from a study funded by \uc2 Medtronic\uc2  (MDT) support validity of the company's treatment for drug-resistant high blood pressure, BMO Capital Markets says in a note. Still, firm notes that reimbursement hurdles for the procedure are high. The MDT results, presented at a medical meeting Sunday, showed a reduction in blood pressure and no significant side effects. The market for high blood pressure treatment is considered to have multi-billion-dollar market potential, though analysts think it will develop slowly. MDT expects approval in its fiscal year 2015. MDT up 2.9% to $39.81. (anjali.athavaley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:18 (Dow Jones) After climbing steadily during the Fed chairman's earlier cautious assessment of the US labor market, the safe-haven market has slipped back near the largest declines of the day. Helping this move, the Dallas Fed showed continued expansion (albeit slower) in its region's manufacturing activity. Benchmark 10-year notes down 11/32 to yield 2.280%, 30-year bonds down 1 1/32 to yield 3.37%. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:16 (Dow Jones) The euro's climb above Y110 has been a major driver of the euro's advance against the dollar today, says \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped above $1.33 and hit its highest level since March 1; it was recently at $1.3327, according to EBS via CQG. (stephen.bernard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:13 (Dow Jones) The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold Treasurys due between February and July of next year. Banks put up $80.029B worth of bids. The sales \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is having little impact on the market. Short-dates notes are flat on the session, while longer-dated bonds have slipped back to the lows of the day. Benchmark 10-year notes down 10/32 to yield 2.277%. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:12 (Dow Jones) As talk continues on how quickly \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  (MS) might further build upon its 51% stake in \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  Smith Barney, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  estimates \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's (C) 49% holding of the retail brokerage being worth $9-11B. Depending on whether it buys just another 14% stake this year or gets Fed clearance to buy all of it, an increase would boost MS' earnings an estimated 4-12%, based on \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 's 2013 EPS estimate. However, and increase could reduce MS' tangible book value 3-15% and lower its Tier 1 common ratio 0.25-0.75 percentage point under Basel III, depending on the stake size and price paid. For C, shedding all of MSSB would cut annual earnings $550M but boost Tier 1 some 0.85 point, says \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 . (brett.philbin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:10 (Dow Jones) Colombian peso trades nearly flat despite a spate of headwinds that in theory should be weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . First, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its key rate unchanged Friday at 5.25%, a decision that should at least deter some capital inflows into the country to benefit from the higher yield in Colombia than in other international markets. Additionally, Finance Minister Juan Carlos Echeverry said in an interview with local media today that he wants to step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Peso has taken little notice and trades at COP1,758.88 to the dollar from COP1,760.4 a day earlier. (darcy.crowe@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Equities Market Talk Editors, \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Paul Vigna, 212 416-2184,paul.vigna@dowjones.com \par Visit the Market Talk website at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-26-12 1141ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120326e83q000c6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
