\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan sees upward pressure on yen waning\b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2012\par 08:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * MOF says to respond to \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility with sense of urgency\par \par \uc2 * G20 discusses \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, may mention it in communized\par \par \uc2 * BOJ gov keeps watch on monetary policy effects on crude oil\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Feb 25 (Reuters) - A senior Japanese Finance Ministry official said the upward pressure on the yen was easing and he saw nothing strange in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movements as it pulls away from record highs below 80 yen versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The official, speaking after the first day of the weekend gathering of Group of 20 finance ministers and central bankers, said the yen was not discussed at the meeting which was dominated by talks on the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 But the G20 did discuss volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as crude oil prices, the official said, adding that these issues may be mentioned in the communique expected at the end of the meeting on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude futures settled near a 10-month high above $125 a barrel on Friday on heightened concerns over tensions with Iran about its nuclear program.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities will continue to respond to excess volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added, signalling readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if speculators push up the yen too high again to deal a blow to the export-reliant economy.\par \par \uc2 "We hear opinions overall, including at deputies' meeting, that volatility exists in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, so I expect (G20) may mention that volatility warants close monitoring," the official said.\par \par \uc2 "We have said that (the yen's) moves have been excessive including before and after (last year's) earthquake, which was not reflecting economic fundamentals. But I see nothing strange in the current movement," he added.\par \par \uc2 The yen, meanwhile, tumbled across the board, a downtrend that started with the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's recent monetary easing. Japan's trade deficit, widening interest rate differentials with the United States favoring the dollar and rising crude oil prices also have hurt the yen's prospects.\par \par \uc2 The dollar hit a fresh 7-1/2-month high of 81.062 yen\par \par \uc2 on trading platform EBS and was last 80.990, away from 75.31 yen hit last October when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to protect exporters and drew criticism from the United States.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , along with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. Federal Reserve, is taking unconventional steps to boost the economy. The BOJ boosted asset purchases by 10 trillion yen on Feb. 14 and pledged to keep ultra-easy policy until a 1 percent inflation goal is in sight.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor \uc2 Masaaki Shirakawa\uc2  said on Saturday that policymakers were also closely watching the effects of monetary easing on crude prices.\par \par \uc2 But he said he did not see monetary easing as a big factor and the recent spike was more due to geopolitical tensions and some bright spots in advanced economies after the New Year.\par \par \uc2 "Generally speaking, we'll closely watch effects and side-effects of monetary easing," he said.\par \par \uc2 (Additional writing by Krista Hughes; Editing by Ed Lane)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 1) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | G | RBN | J | RNP | DNP | PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120226e82q00033\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
