\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Japan MOF official: nothing strange in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  moves\b0\par\par\uc2 486 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2012\par 09:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Sees speculation persisting, to respond as appropriate\par \par \uc2 * Yen at 6-month low vs dollar, 3-month low vs euro\par \par \uc2 * Yen has been weakening since BOJ surprise easing\par \par \uc2 * Risk appetite also improving after Greek bailout\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 22 (Reuters) - Japan's government saw nothing strange in recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves that saw the yen hit a six-month low versus the dollar and a three-month low versus the euro, a senior official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The yen has been edging lower since the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  surprised investors last week with additional monetary easing, offering a respite for policy-makers who worry that a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depresses exports and harms the economy.\par \par \uc2 But the official said market speculation that could contribute to the yen's rise is persisting and Japan will continue to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves and respond as appropriate.\par \par \uc2 "The situation remains unchanged in that if the yen rises it could push down the Japanese economy, and market speculation that could contribute to the yen's rises is persisting," the official told reporters on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 "We have been strongly concerned about whether one-sided yen rises since last summer were reflecting economic fundamentals. I don't see anything strange in the underlying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements."\par \par \uc2 The dollar traded around 80.04 yen on Wednesday, rising above 80 yen for the first time since August 2011. The euro rose to 106.145 yen, its highest since mid-November, in the wake of the official's comments.\par \par \uc2 The yen's weakening was due to the BOJ's easing last week and the euro zone's agreement on a Greek rescue package on Monday, the official said.\par \par \uc2 In a surprise move, the BOJ on Feb. 14 boosted asset purchases and set an inflation goal of 1 percent, pledging to keep ultra-easy policy until that price level is in sight.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the BOJ's easing, the yen has come under pressure this month after data showed that Japan's current account surplus -- a major and constant support for the yen -- fell to a 15-year low last year.\par \par \uc2 Japan spent a record 8 trillion yen ($100 billion) in unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Oct. 31, and another 1 trillion yen in early November on undeclared forays into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 In August, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold roughly 4.5 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , far exceeding the 2.1 trillion yen it sold on Sept. 15, 2010.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Treasury criticised the solo \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a report last year, saying markets were not moving in a disorderly manner, while other Group of Seven countries also have taken a dim view of Japan's solo action.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 79.7500 Japanese yen)\par \par \uc2 (Additional writing by Stanley White; Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -JAPAN/MOF (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120225e82m0006m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
