\par\par \b \uc2 DJ WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Gains On Greek Bailout Hopes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Walter   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2012\par 00:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--The euro strengthened Friday on hopes that the complex negotiations over a new debt relief package for Greece were coming together ahead of a Monday meeting of euro-zone finance ministers. The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rallied 4.2% against the dollar since touching its lowest level in more than 16 months in January.\par \par \uc2 Reports that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchanged Greek bonds Friday to ensure that its holdings wouldn't be subject to the same restructuring planned for private bond holders bolstered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Though some investors complained that the special treatment for the ECB would discourage further investment in euro zone bonds by subordinating private sector creditors, most took the mere presence of a deal as a sign of progress in the long-stalled talks to resolve Greece's debt problems.\par \par \uc2 The euro has traded in a relatively narrow range in recent weeks as talks have dragged on between Greece, its public sector European creditors, and private bondholders over a EUR130 billion bailout needed for the country to avoid a default next month.\par \par \uc2 "This is being read by the market as paving the way for a restructuring next week, so that was supportive, but it's still not 100% that its going to happen," said Ron Leven, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.3139 from $1.3130 late Thursday, according to EBS via CQG. The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at Y104.54 from Y103.67.\par \par \uc2 After months of painstaking negotiations fraught with constant delays, investors remain cautious about next week's meetings. Even if negotiators are able to achieve a deal, a stagnating European economy, coupled with the possibility of more debt talks in other peripheral European countries, may weigh on the euro in the coming weeks, said Marc Chandler, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 . He sees the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening to $1.20 by the middle of the year.\par \par \uc2 "Even if this program works, you are looking at a prolonged period of weak growth in Europe, and you are looking at further expansion of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's balance sheet," he said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar had its second weekly gain against the Japanese yen, climbing to its highest level since the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last October. Improving economic economic data in the U.S. and efforts by the Bank of Japan to stimulate its economy by increasing liquidity are both helping to support the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Conference Board reported Friday that its index of leading economic indicators in January increased for the fourth consecutive month, and the Labor Department said that consumer prices rose 0.2% last month, less than expected.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at Y79.58 from Y78.93 and at CHF0.9200 from CHF0.9190.\par \par \uc2 The U.K. pound was at $1.5828 from $1.5799. The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at about 79.392 from about 79.348.\par \par \uc2 -By Matthew Walter, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2910; matt.walter@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 - -\par 