\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA: When Looking For Signs Of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Don't Focus Only On Financing Bills\b0\par\par\uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2012\par 09:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Short-term debt not only way \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  finances \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- History shows \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  could borrow money from \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- MOF's remaining firepower estimated around Y70 trillion, strategists say\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 )--In trying to divine whether Japan would again wade into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to push the yen lower, traders and analysts have been watching the government's financing bills in the belief that without the cash they secure, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't an option.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But history shows the real story is slightly different.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While so-called financing bills remain the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's main funding tool for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the ministry has used other means to raise the funds, including a trip to the bank--the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Other than issuing financing bills, we also have other options for raising the funds while making sure not to affect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market," a ministry official told \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For now, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in any case appears to be off the cards. After this week's surprise easing move by the BOJ and signs of a stronger U.S. economy, the dollar climbed to Y79.18 on Friday, its highest level since Oct. 31 when a fall to a post-war record low of Y75.31 prompted large-scale \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the ministry.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The most recent case of borrowing funds from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  goes back to 2003. The ministry and the bank announced in December of that year that the ministry could take advantage of a repurchase agreement with the BOJ to sell up to Y10 trillion in U.S. Treasurys with a three-month buyback period.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the time Japan had spent Y20.4 trillion through 2003 trying to weaken the yen in frequent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The ministry used the money as part of yen selling totaling Y14.83 trillion in the first quarter of 2004, still the largest on record for any three-month period by Japan. The financing bills needed for the more conventional funding approach were still tied up in parliament.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The step was unusual, but it was in no way reckless, according to Koji Fukaya, director of fixed income at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It wasn't something that damaged authorities' credibility," he said. "I don't believe the BOJ showed any reluctance in taking part."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The same funding tool was even more common in the pre-floating days before the 1971 collapse of the Bretton Woods system. With rates fixed, authorities seeking to keep their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in line could only use \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . At that time the dollar was at a now-distant Y360.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At present, there is no BOJ-MOF agreement in place, although formulating a new one could likely be agreed upon quickly.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since September 2010 when \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  resumed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the first time in six and half years, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has spent Y16.5 trillion in yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Right after the October-November \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Y9.1 trillion, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had only around Y25 trillion in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war chest, prompting strategists' discussions about whether \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would need to refrain from further yen selling. The amount is now estimated around Y70 trillion, thanks to two extra budgets passed in November and earlier this month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Whether to resort to short-term asset sales is in any case up to Finance Minister Jun Azumi, and traders say it could be used to add to the surprise factor in any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's hard to say how the market will react if this is announced, but non-Japanese investors may be quite surprised," said a Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 17-02-12 0823GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4258 5095   \