er reported a record profit of $7.6 billion for 2011, but saw losses in Europe and thin profit margins in the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ASIAN STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets rose Friday on upbeat U.S. economic data and signs of progress in Greece's efforts to avoid a debt default, with a weaker yen propelling Tokyo stocks higher, while the Seoul market raced to six-month highs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors were encouraged by news that the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to swap its Greek debt holdings for new bonds once debt restructuring negotiations are complete, moving Athens a step closer to securing a second bailout package critical to avoiding a default.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A batch of U.S. housing, jobless and manufacturing data showing strength in the world's biggest economy lifted the mood as well.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The U.S. continues to be one of the brighter spots in the global economy," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note. It added that while risks abound, "Greece is less likely to deliver a scare to the markets, which already seem to be pricing in quite a negative scenario."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DJIA futures were up 8 points in screen trade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Sydney, \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANZ Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 1.5% after it posted a 4.1% rise in underlying earnings for the first quarter, impressing some analysts with its profit margin.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen's continued weakness against the U.S. dollar further lifted the country's exporter stocks, a sector that's suffered heavily due to the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's persistent strength in the past year. The yen selling was triggered by the Bank of Japan's unexpected move this week to expand its assets purchase plan and formalize an inflation target.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sony\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 2.2%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  advanced 1.8% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Honda Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  gained 2.2%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Billabong International\f28 \uc2 \f2  rocketed 48% to A$2.65 after the Australian clothing and surfware retailer rejected a conditional A$3-a-share takeover bid from \f28 \uc2 \f2 TPG Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and instead decided to proceed with the partial sale of Nixon Inc.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The partial sale represents an enterprise value of about US$464 million.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Seoul market rose to a six-month high as the upbeat U.S. data raised hopes of a demand uptick for its big exporters. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics\f28 \uc2 \f2  climbed 2.8%.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was steady against the U.S. dollar and consolidated in a tight range as investors looked to developments in the Greek debt saga.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is still the issue of an acceptable mechanism for monitoring the implementation of the accord in Greece. There may more discussion at Monday's Euro group meeting, but no resolution is likely," Brown Brother Harriman said in a note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was at $1.3128 against the greenback, from $1.3135 late Thursday in New York, and at Y103.82, from Y103.60. The BOJ's action continued to hurt the yen as it skirted three-and-a-half-month lows against the dollar, with the greenback tapping Y79.13 early Friday, its highest since the Oct. 31 yen selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It was recently at Y79.07, from Y78.94.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par METALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold was at $1,729.10 a troy ounce, up 30 cents from its New York settlement Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL SUMMARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March Nymex crude oil futures, which tapped multiweek highs Thursday, added 5 cents to $102.36 a barrel on Globex.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES \par German Move Lifts Greek Bailout Hopes \par Survey Finds Dealers Underestimated Coming Rate Shift \par US Data Indicate Continuing Economic Recovery \par ECB Swapping Existing Greek Bond Holdings For Newly Issued Greek Bonds -SourceGerman President Wulff Being Investigated \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Eyes European Banks For Downgrade \par GM Profit Falls, Hit By Europe Losses \par Icahn Makes Hostile $2.6B Bid For \f28 \uc2 \f2 CVR Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par Bill Gross's Dual Play In Treasury Bonds Pays Off \par Portugal's Largest Union Calls General Strike \par INTERVIEW: Ruling Party Anti-Deflation Panel Applauds Latest BOJ Easing \par Nintendo Teams Up With Hulu Plus To Offer TV Shows, Classic Movies On Wii Console \par NEC Outlines Early Retirement Plan, Overtime Pay Cuts -Nikkei \par Takeda To Debut Five Drugs In Rapid Succession -Nikkei \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Motors\f28 \uc2 \f2  To Give Russia 1st Crack At New SUV -Nikkei \par Japan, China Roll Up Sleeves For Yen-Yuan Exchanges -Nikkei \par GS Yuasa To Open Auto Lithium Battery Plant In March -Nikkei \par Japan-China Trade Surged 14% To Record High In '11 -Nikkei \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 17-02-12 0300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62500   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120217e82h0004g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
