\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Fin Min Remarks Perplex Market\b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2012\par 10:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Japanese Finance Minister Jun Azumi makes comments that some interpreted as revealing details of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --Azumi and officials later deny that comments were meant to refer to specific \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels\par \par \uc2 --Azumi also says \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own if needed to curb the yen's strength\par \par \uc2 TOKYO -- Japanese Finance Minister Jun Azumi perplexed the markets on Friday with comments that were interpreted by some as revealing rarely disclosed details about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Grilled in parliament about the effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October to tame the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, Azumi touched on specific yen-sale levels, but later said he was merely repeating figures put forth by an opposition lawmaker.\par \par \uc2 "It was a complete slip of the tongue, and it was shocking that the finance minister mentioned a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level which he never should," said Yuzo Sakai, senior trader at Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Ueda Harlow.\par \par \uc2 In response to the question by Yasutoshi Nishimura, Azumi said he instructed that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  be carried out when the dollar fell to Y75.63, referring to a number shown on a table Nishimura was using to illustrate the yen's moves at the time.\par \par \uc2 "I instructed that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  be carried out at Y75.63, as shown at the very top of lawmaker Nishimura's table," Azumi said.\par \par \uc2 Nishimura's table listed the dollar's closing rate against the yen in the days before and after the Oct. 31 Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Y75.63 figure was shown at the top of the list as the closing rate for Oct. 30.\par \par \uc2 Nishimura asked Azumi whether he was satisfied with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding how it had pushed the dollar back up to Y78.20, referring to the closing rate on Nov. 5, the day after Japan stopped the latest yen-selling campaign.\par \par \uc2 Azumi said he believed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which went on for six days and in which \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent over Y9.0 trillion, was effective.\par \par \uc2 "Regarding the question whether I am satisfied after we stopped at Y78.20.. I believe that it was effective to a certain extent," the finance minister said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates hardly reacted to the comments with the dollar remaining largely in a narrow band between Y77.50 and Y77.70, but the Nikkei ran a story on the front page of its evening edition with the headline: "Instructed at Y75.30, stopped at Y78.20."\par \par \uc2 Azumi, clearly irked by the media reports, later tried to clarify his comments by saying that he was merely reading what was shown on Nishimura's table and not referring to a particular level at which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was carried out.\par \par \uc2 "Haven't you seen the parliamentary session? I said those things just because I was shown the board with exchange rates on the day of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the day it ended," he told reporters back at the finance ministry.\par \par \uc2 "Let me make this clear to you. I didn't talk about any levels at all. Period."\par \par \uc2 And while they were overshadowed by the comments on the specific \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, Azumi did tell parliament that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained determined to take action, even on its own, to curb the yen's rise if needed.\par \par \uc2 "If speculators are moving exchange rates through their speculative actions, I will not hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That means that I will not at all hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unilaterally," Azumi said, using some of his strongest language to date to counter speculation that U.S. and European opposition might tie Tokyo's hands over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Mario Draghi on Thursday joined the U.S. in signaling objection to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's solo yen sales, telling a news conference that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be implemented in a multilateral fashion. The U.S. Treasury made it clear in a report on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last year that it didn't back Tokyo's solo actions in August and October.\par \par \uc2 -By George Nishiyama and Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; +81-3-6269-2818; george.nishiyama@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -Takashi Mochizuki contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 10, 2012 04:35 ET (09:35 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120210e82a002q6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
