\par\par \b \uc2 DJ WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Touches Two-Month High On Greek Hopes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Walter   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2012\par 23:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--The euro surged to a two-month high against the dollar Thursday on signs an agreement was at hand for emergency funding needed to avert a Greek default.\par \par \uc2 Following weeks of negotiations, Greek Prime Minister Lucas Papademos reached a deal with the country's main political parties Thursday on spending and wage cuts required for EUR130 billion ($172.7 billion) in aid from the European Commission, the International Monetary Fund and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro rose to an intraday peak of $1.3322, its highest level since Dec. 12.\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed some of those gains after the IMF said it may require Greece to follow through with agreed-upon economic changes before contributing to the bailout.\par \par \uc2 Better-than-expected economic data from the U.S. and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to hold interest rates steady also helped the euro, as increasing optimism about the global economic outlook boosted investors' desire to hold risky-seeming assets.\par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Mario Draghi said there were "signs of stabilization" in the euro zone, which some investors took as a sign policy makers will forgo rate cuts for the rest of the year.\par \par \uc2 "Draghi's tone was increasingly confident," Andrew Wilkinson, chief economic strategist at Miller Tabak & Co., said. "Everything we're hearing from the ECB is relatively bullish."\par \par \uc2 The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at $1.3285 from $1.3260 late Wednesday, and Y103.18 from Y102.16, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., the Labor Department announced jobless claims were lower than forecast last week and the Commerce Department said inventory growth in December exceeded expectations. That sent the dollar down against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as investors emerged from safe-haven bets taken when the economic recovery looked less certain.\par \par \uc2 The yen was one of the few \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lose ground against the dollar. Earlier this week, government data showed the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had used "stealth" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  following its eight trillion yen sale Oct. 31. That raised the prospect of Japan stepping into the market again in the future, should the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain near record highs.\par \par \uc2 "The market has seen that they have no problem \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  quietly," said Kathy Lien, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at GFT \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The yen also was weakened by a government report showing Japan's current-account surplus shrank 43.9% last year.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at Y77.66 from Y77.05 and at CHF0.9118 from CHF0.9124. The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at about 78.594 from about 78.641.\par \par \uc2 The U.K. pound was at $1.5824 from $1.5818, after the Bank of England said it would begin another round of bond buying to stimulate the economy.\par \par \uc2 -By Matthew Walter, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2910; matt.walter@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Javier E. David contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020120209e82900bf5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
