\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2012\par 10:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CONCESSION SMOOTHS WAY TOWARD GREEK DEBT DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made key concessions over its holdings of Greek government bonds, which will contribute to a reduction of the country's debt burden and smooth the path toward a new bailout for the country, said people briefed on Greece's debt-restructuring negotiations. (published 0054 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: GERMAN EXPORTS FELL IN DECEMBER, TRADE SURPLUS NARROWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German exports fell in December, decreasing after November's gain, and narrowing Germany's trade surplus, data from the Federal Statistics Office, or Destatis, showed Wednesday. (published 0725 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: FRANCE 2011 STATE BUDGET GAP EUR90.8B VS EUR148.8B 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 France's central state budget deficit narrowed in 2011 to EUR90.8 billion from EUR148.8 billion in 2010, the budget ministry said Wednedsay. (published 0746 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREEK PM TO MEET PARTY LEADERS ON LOAN DEAL 1300 GMT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greek Prime Minister Lucas Papdemos is scheduled Wednesday to meet with party leaders on reforms demanded by international creditors in exchange for a second bailout at 1300 GMT, the prime minister's office said. (published 0150 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATASNAP: SPAIN DEC INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT -3.7% ON YEAR VS -7% NOV \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spanish industrial production continued to fall in December as weak domestic consumption and slack export markets undermined demand for manufactured goods. (published 0814 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN DEC TRADE FIGURES POINT TO DECLINE IN Q4 GDP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany's December trade figures are pointing to a decline in the country's total output reading in last year's fourth quarter. (published 0056 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA INCREASES PRESENCE IN JAPAN DEBT MARKET, BOJ CALLS FOR FURTHER REFORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China greatly increased its presence in the Japanese debt market last year, tripling its trading volume from the previous year, a move likely to give ammunition to those calling on Beijing to open up its own financial markets to outside investors. (published 0113 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA YUAN UP LATE ON PBOC GUIDANCE, GREEK OPTIMISM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's yuan rose against the U.S. dollar late Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a significantly more bullish reference exchange rate for the local unit on the back of the euro's strong gains overnight. (published 0118 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF FRANCE SURVEY SEES 0% 1Q FRENCH GDP GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A survey of business managers by the Bank of France Wednesday forecast zero growth in the first quarter of 2012. (published 0730 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUNGARY FOREIGN MIN: HOPE TO START IMF/EU TALKS BY MARCH-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungary's Foreign Minister Janos Martonyi said his country hopes to start negotiations with the European Union and the International Monetary Fund on new financial assistance by the beginning of March at the latest, German daily Financial Times Deutschland reported Wednesday. (published 0821 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN 2011 CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS FALLS AT RECORD RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's current account surplus shrank by its fastest rate on record in 2011, as exports stumbled and energy prices soared, leading to the first shortfall in merchandise trade in decades, government data showed Wednesday. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ DEP GOV: STRICT CHINESE CAPITAL REGULATIONS HINDER INTERNATIONALIZATION OF YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Deputy Gov. Kiyohiko Nishimura said Wednesday that Beijing needs to reduce capital regulations hindering the flow of offshore Chinese yuan back to China if it is to further internationalize its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  FOREIGNERS RAMPED UP JGB BUYING IN 2011 AMID GLOBAL DEBT FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors ramped up purchases of Japanese bonds in 2011, confirming a global risk-aversion trend amid the debt crisis in Europe, and lower ratings on U.S. government bonds. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PARLIAMENT PASSES 4TH EXTRA BUDGET FOR QUAKE-RELIEF MEASURES -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's parliament approved Wednesday a fourth extra budget for the current fiscal year that will assist companies struggling as a result of the March 2011 earthquake and tsunami as well as the recent sharp appreciation of the yen, which has weighed on the country's exports, Kyodo News reported. (published 0701 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA 'BIG FOUR' BANKS ISSUED CNY320 BLN NEW YUAN LOANS IN JAN - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's "Big Four" state-run banks issued a combined CNY320 billion in new yuan loans in January, with the figure for the entire sector likely reaching CNY800 billion, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Wednesday, citing unnamed persons familiar with the situation. (published 0316 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par POLITICAL STRAINS COULD SLOW ASIA'S RESPONSE TO ECONOMIC SHOCK - S&P \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Policymakers in Asia may not be nimble enough to respond to a potential global recession, given political constraints in many Asian countries, ratings firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a report. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: EXPECT CHINA PROPERTY CONSTRUCTION TO SLOW AMID GOVERNMENT TIGHTENING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property construction in China will likely slow down due to government tightening measures, which could have an impact on economic growth this year, Andrew Colquhoun, Fitch Ratings' head of Asia-Pacific sovereign ratings, said Wednesday. (published 0212 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: EURO WILL BE LESS ATTRACTIVE RESERVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNTIL CRISIS RESOLVED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro will be a less attractive reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  until the debt crisis resolved, Andrew Colquhoun, Fitch's head of Asia-Pacific sovereign ratings, said Wednesday. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: DON'T EXPECT CHINA TO PROVIDE LOTS OF MONEY TO EURO BAILOUT FUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is unlikely to provide lots of money suddenly to the European Financial Stability Facility, the euro zone's bailout fund, although China needs euro-denominated assets to diversify its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  portfolio, Tony Stringer, global head of sovereign ratings for Fitch, said Wednesday. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: 1H GROWTH LIKELY LESS THAN 1% VS 2H 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan late Tuesday said economic growth in the first half will likely be less than 1% sequentially compared with the second half of 2011. (published 2323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOK BOARD MEMBER: YUAN UNLIKELY TO BECOME WORLD RESERVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan isn't likely to become one of the world's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of choice in the near future unless the Chinese authorities adopt a more free floating exchange rate system, a member of the Bank of Korea's monetary policy board said Wednesday. (published 0810 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE ECONOMIC CHIEF: 1Q GDP GROWTH LIKELY STRONGER THAN 4.6% IN 1Q 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines' economic growth in the first quarter will likely be stronger than the 4.6% growth in the first quarter of last year amid accelerated government spending, Economic Planning Secretary Cayetano Paderanga said Wednesday. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA DEPUTY GOVERNOR: STILL MONITORING INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia is still monitoring price pressures even though inflation in January came in at the lower end of the bank's target range, a deputy governor said Wednesday. (published 0621 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: MALAYSIA'S INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY GREW 1.7% ON YEAR IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's industrial output growth likely weakened in December as global demand for the country's products slowed. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: MALAYSIA'S DECEMBER EXPORTS LIKELY UP 5.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's export growth likely slowed in December, hurt by weaker demand from advanced economies due to the European debt crisis. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S SECRET YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COULD BE TEMPLATE FOR FUTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's disclosure Tuesday that it secretly sold yen for several days in November has been followed by relative stability in the yen's exchange rate. That has prompted analysts to suggest an invisible-hand approach might be a better alternative to massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that ultimately fall short. (published 2350 GMT) [ 08-02-12 0956GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120208e828000sp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
