YUAN LOANS IN JAN - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's "Big Four" state-run banks issued a combined CNY320 billion in new yuan loans in January, with the figure for the entire sector likely reaching CNY800 billion, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Wednesday, citing unnamed persons familiar with the situation. (published 0316 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par POLITICAL STRAINS COULD SLOW ASIA'S RESPONSE TO ECONOMIC SHOCK - S&P \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Policymakers in Asia may not be nimble enough to respond to a potential global recession, given political constraints in many Asian countries, ratings firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a report. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: EXPECT CHINA PROPERTY CONSTRUCTION TO SLOW AMID GOVERNMENT TIGHTENING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property construction in China will likely slow down due to government tightening measures, which could have an impact on economic growth this year, Andrew Colquhoun, Fitch Ratings' head of Asia-Pacific sovereign ratings, said Wednesday. (published 0212 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: EURO WILL BE LESS ATTRACTIVE RESERVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNTIL CRISIS RESOLVED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro will be a less attractive reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  until the debt crisis resolved, Andrew Colquhoun, Fitch's head of Asia-Pacific sovereign ratings, said Wednesday. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: DON'T EXPECT CHINA TO PROVIDE LOTS OF MONEY TO EURO BAILOUT FUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is unlikely to provide lots of money suddenly to the European Financial Stability Facility, the euro zone's bailout fund, although China needs euro-denominated assets to diversify its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  portfolio, Tony Stringer, global head of sovereign ratings for Fitch, said Wednesday. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: 1H GROWTH LIKELY LESS THAN 1% VS 2H 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan late Tuesday said economic growth in the first half will likely be less than 1% sequentially compared with the second half of 2011. (published 2323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE ECONOMIC CHIEF: 1Q GDP GROWTH LIKELY STRONGER THAN 4.6% IN 1Q 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines' economic growth in the first quarter will likely be stronger than the 4.6% growth in the first quarter of last year amid accelerated government spending, Economic Planning Secretary Cayetano Paderanga said Wednesday. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA DEPUTY GOVERNOR: STILL MONITORING INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia is still monitoring price pressures even though inflation in January came in at the lower end of the bank's target range, a deputy governor said Wednesday. (published 0621 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM JANUARY VEHICLE SALES DOWN 60% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vehicle sales in Vietnam fell 60% in January from a year earlier, the fourth straight monthly decline, industry data showed Wednesday. (published 0552 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NATIONAL AUSTRALIA BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRICES A$1.5B 2017 NOTES AT SWAP +185 BPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 National Australia Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , one of the country's four largest lenders, on Wednesday priced A$1.5 billion in fixed and floating rate 2017 notes, reopening the market to unsecured debt in 2012. (published 0528 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KERRY PROPERTIES SEEKS TO PRICE US$300M-US$400M BOND TO YIELD AROUND TSYS +462.5 BPS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kerry Properties\f28 \uc2 \f2  is seeking to price today a US$300 million-US$400 million dollar bond to yield around 462.5 basis points over comparable U.S. Treasurys, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Wednesday. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SHUI ON LAND SEEKS TO PRICE 3-YEAR DOLLAR BOND TO YIELD AROUND 9.75% - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shui On Land Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to sell a three-year U.S. dollar bond, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Wednesday. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: MALAYSIA'S INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY GREW 1.7% ON YEAR IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's industrial output growth likely weakened in December as global demand for the country's products slowed. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: MALAYSIA'S DECEMBER EXPORTS LIKELY UP 5.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's export growth likely slowed in December, hurt by weaker demand from advanced economies due to the European debt crisis. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S SECRET YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COULD BE TEMPLATE FOR FUTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's disclosure Tuesday that it secretly sold yen for several days in November has been followed by relative stability in the yen's exchange rate. That has prompted analysts to suggest an invisible-hand approach might be a better alternative to massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that ultimately fall short. (published 2350 GMT) [ 08-02-12 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120208e828000g7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
