million dollar bond to yield around 462.5 basis points over comparable U.S. Treasurys, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Wednesday. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: MALAYSIA'S INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY GREW 1.7% ON YEAR IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's industrial output growth likely weakened in December as global demand for the country's products slowed. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: MALAYSIA'S DECEMBER EXPORTS LIKELY UP 5.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's export growth likely slowed in December, hurt by weaker demand from advanced economies due to the European debt crisis. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S SECRET YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COULD BE TEMPLATE FOR FUTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's disclosure Tuesday that it secretly sold yen for several days in November has been followed by relative stability in the yen's exchange rate. That has prompted analysts to suggest an invisible-hand approach might be a better alternative to massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that ultimately fall short. (published 2350 GMT) [ 08-02-12 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120208e828000bs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
