\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 941 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2012\par 06:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: JAPAN'S 2011 CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS FALLS AT RECORD RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's current account surplus shrank by its fastest rate on record in 2011, as exports stumbled and energy prices soared, leading to the first shortfall in merchandise trade in decades, government data showed Wednesday. (published 0342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ DEP GOV: STRICT CHINESE CAPITAL REGULATIONS HINDER INTERNATIONALIZATION OF YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Deputy Gov. Kiyohiko Nishimura said Wednesday that Beijing needs to reduce capital regulations hindering the flow of offshore Chinese yuan back to China if it is to further internationalize its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: EXPECT CHINA PROPERTY CONSTRUCTION TO SLOW AMID GOVERNMENT TIGHTENING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property construction in China will likely slow down due to government tightening measures, which could have an impact on economic growth this year, Andrew Colquhoun, Fitch Ratings' head of Asia-Pacific sovereign ratings, said Wednesday. (published 0212 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: EURO WILL BE LESS ATTRACTIVE RESERVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNTIL CRISIS RESOLVED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro will be a less attractive reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  until the debt crisis resolved, Andrew Colquhoun, Fitch's head of Asia-Pacific sovereign ratings, said Wednesday. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: DON'T EXPECT CHINA TO PROVIDE LOTS OF MONEY TO EURO BAILOUT FUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is unlikely to provide lots of money suddenly to the European Financial Stability Facility, the euro zone's bailout fund, although China needs euro-denominated assets to diversify its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  portfolio, Tony Stringer, global head of sovereign ratings for Fitch, said Wednesday. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par POLITICAL STRAINS COULD SLOW ASIA'S RESPONSE TO ECONOMIC SHOCK - S&P \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Policymakers in Asia may not be nimble enough to respond to a potential global recession, given political constraints in many Asian countries, ratings firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a report. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ 2ND UPDATE: CONCESSION SMOOTHS WAY TOWARD GREEK DEBT DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made key concessions over its holdings of Greek government bonds, which will contribute to a reduction of the country's debt burden and smooth the path toward a new bailout for the country, said people briefed on Greece's debt-restructuring negotiations. (published 0054 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN JAN 1-20 TRADE DEFICIT Y1.560 TLN; UP 102.1% ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan posted a merchandise trade deficit of Y1.560 trillion in the first 20 days of January, up 102.1% from the Y771.89 billion deficit in the year-earlier period, the finance ministry said Wednesday. (published 0004 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: FOREIGNERS RAMPED UP JGB BUYING IN 2011 AMID GLOBAL DEBT FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors ramped up purchases of Japanese bonds in 2011, confirming a global risk-aversion trend amid the debt crisis in Europe, and lower ratings on U.S. government bonds. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA 'BIG FOUR' BANKS ISSUED CNY320 BILLION NEW YUAN LOANS IN JAN -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's "Big Four" state-run banks issued around CNY320 billion combined in new yuan loans in January, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Wednesday, without citing sources. (published 2329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN SAYS SURPLUS WILL GIVE RBA ROOM ON RATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia Treasurer Wayne Swan Wednesday said a return to surplus will enable the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lower rates. (published 2231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA BANKS' HOUSEHOLD LOANS FALL BY RECORD AMOUNT IN JANUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean banks' lending to households fell the most on record in January because of lower mortgage loans amid sluggish housing transactions, the Bank of Korea said Wednesday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: 1H GROWTH LIKELY LESS THAN 1% VS 2H 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan late Tuesday said economic growth in the first half will likely be less than 1% sequentially compared with the second half of 2011. (published 2323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE ECONOMIC CHIEF: 1Q GDP GROWTH LIKELY STRONGER THAN 4.6% IN 1Q 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines' economic growth in the first quarter will likely be stronger than the 4.6% growth in the first quarter of last year amid accelerated government spending, Economic Planning Secretary Cayetano Paderanga said Wednesday. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KERRY PROPERTIES SEEKS TO PRICE US$300M-US$400M BOND TO YIELD AROUND TSYS +462.5 BPS - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kerry Properties\f28 \uc2 \f2  is seeking to price today a US$300 million-US$400 million dollar bond to yield around 462.5 basis points over comparable U.S. Treasurys, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Wednesday. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BDO UNIBANK SETS $300 MILLION BOND COUPON AT 4.5%, YIELD AT 4.625% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine lender BDO Unibank Inc. Wednesday fixed the coupon for its $300 million five-year, fixed-rate, U.S. dollar-denominated bond at 4.5%, with the yield set at 4.625%. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par      ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: MALAYSIA'S INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT LIKELY GREW 1.7% ON YEAR IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's industrial output growth likely weakened in December as global demand for the country's products slowed. (published 0417 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: MALAYSIA'S DECEMBER EXPORTS LIKELY UP 5.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's export growth likely slowed in December, hurt by weaker demand from advanced economies due to the European debt crisis. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S SECRET YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COULD BE TEMPLATE FOR FUTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's disclosure Tuesday that it secretly sold yen for several days in November has been followed by relative stability in the yen's exchange rate. That has prompted analysts to suggest an invisible-hand approach might be a better alternative to massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that ultimately fall short. (published 2350 GMT) [ 08-02-12 0502GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120208e8280008p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
