\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 799 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2012\par 05:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: JAPAN'S 2011 CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS FALLS AT RECORD RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's current account surplus shrank by its fastest rate on record in 2011, as exports stumbled and energy prices soared, leading to the first shortfall in merchandise trade in decades, government data showed Wednesday. (published 0342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ DEP GOV: STRICT CHINESE CAPITAL REGULATIONS HINDER INTERNATIONALIZATION OF YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Deputy Gov. Kiyohiko Nishimura said Wednesday that Beijing needs to reduce capital regulations hindering the flow of offshore Chinese yuan back to China if it is to further internationalize its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: EXPECT CHINA PROPERTY CONSTRUCTION TO SLOW AMID GOVERNMENT TIGHTENING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Property construction in China will likely slow down due to government tightening measures, which could have an impact on economic growth this year, Andrew Colquhoun, Fitch Ratings' head of Asia-Pacific sovereign ratings, said Wednesday. (published 0212 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH ANALYST: EURO WILL BE LESS ATTRACTIVE RESERVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNTIL CRISIS RESOLVED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro will be a less attractive reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  until the debt crisis resolved, Andrew Colquhoun, Fitch's head of Asia-Pacific sovereign ratings, said Wednesday. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par POLITICAL STRAINS COULD SLOW ASIA'S RESPONSE TO ECONOMIC SHOCK - S&P \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Policymakers in Asia may not be nimble enough to respond to a potential global recession, given political constraints in many Asian countries, ratings firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a report. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ 2ND UPDATE: CONCESSION SMOOTHS WAY TOWARD GREEK DEBT DEAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made key concessions over its holdings of Greek government bonds, which will contribute to a reduction of the country's debt burden and smooth the path toward a new bailout for the country, said people briefed on Greece's debt-restructuring negotiations. (published 0054 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: GREECE DELAYS TALKS ON POLITICAL DEAL ON REFORMS AMID STRIKES, PROTESTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A meeting between Greek Prime Minister Lucas Papademos and the three party bosses supporting his coalition government over a new loan deal for the country has been pushed back for yet another day as the government continued efforts to finalize a raft of painful reforms. (published 2103 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA TO IMPOSE NEW CAPITAL RULES ON BANKS FROM JULY - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will likely implement new regulatory capital requirements for commercial banks from July 1, the 21st Century Business Herald reported Wednesday, citing a person familiar with the situation. (published 0140 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN JAN 1-20 TRADE DEFICIT Y1.560 TLN; UP 102.1% ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan posted a merchandise trade deficit of Y1.560 trillion in the first 20 days of January, up 102.1% from the Y771.89 billion deficit in the year-earlier period, the finance ministry said Wednesday. (published 0004 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: FOREIGNERS RAMPED UP JGB BUYING IN 2011 AMID GLOBAL DEBT FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors ramped up purchases of Japanese bonds in 2011, confirming a global risk-aversion trend amid the debt crisis in Europe, and lower ratings on U.S. government bonds. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA 'BIG FOUR' BANKS ISSUED CNY320 BILLION NEW YUAN LOANS IN JAN -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's "Big Four" state-run banks issued around CNY320 billion combined in new yuan loans in January, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Wednesday, without citing sources. (published 2329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN SAYS SURPLUS WILL GIVE RBA ROOM ON RATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia Treasurer Wayne Swan Wednesday said a return to surplus will enable the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lower rates. (published 2231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA BANKS' HOUSEHOLD LOANS FALL BY RECORD AMOUNT IN JANUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean banks' lending to households fell the most on record in January because of lower mortgage loans amid sluggish housing transactions, the Bank of Korea said Wednesday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: 1H GROWTH LIKELY LESS THAN 1% VS 2H 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan late Tuesday said economic growth in the first half will likely be less than 1% sequentially compared with the second half of 2011. (published 2323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BDO UNIBANK SETS $300 MILLION BOND COUPON AT 4.5%, YIELD AT 4.625% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine lender BDO Unibank Inc. Wednesday fixed the coupon for its $300 million five-year, fixed-rate, U.S. dollar-denominated bond at 4.5%, with the yield set at 4.625%. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par      ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S SECRET YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COULD BE TEMPLATE FOR FUTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's disclosure Tuesday that it secretly sold yen for several days in November has been followed by relative stability in the yen's exchange rate. That has prompted analysts to suggest an invisible-hand approach might be a better alternative to massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that ultimately fall short. (published 2350 GMT) [ 08-02-12 0400GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120208e8280006u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
