\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  FOCUS: Japan Must Be Invoking Greek Deities\b0\par\par\uc2 625 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2012\par 12:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Data shows how difficult BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in October\par \par \uc2 --JPY's continued strength suggests more needed soon\par \par \uc2 --On going Greek uncertainty will make matters worse\par \par \uc2 By Nicholas Hastings\par \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be praying for Greek gods to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yen is already back up close to levels that forced the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to wade into the market at the end of October last year.\par \par \uc2 And, if Greek debt negotiations continue to drag on, market sentiment is likely to deteriorate, putting even more upward pressure on the yen.\par \par \uc2 The dilemma that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  faces in trying to control the yen against market forces was demonstrated by new figures from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These showed that the bank had to spend even more than it has in recent years, Y8.07 trillion on October 31, to push the dollar back up from under Y76 to over Y78.\par \par \uc2 Then, it had to continue selling the yen in smaller amounts over the next four days to discourage any immediate buying of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these cheaper levels.\par \par \uc2 The exercise illustrates the problem any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  faces with unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that tries to buck the trend.\par \par \uc2 The problem for the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  is that this trend could become even more intense and makes its job even more difficult.\par \par \uc2 Over the last few weeks, global risk sentiment has improved but the yen itself has remained strong, spending most of this year trading around the Y77 level to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 This month could bring even more flows in its favor, especially if Japanese companies repatriate overseas earnings ahead of the end of the financial year as they normally do.\par \par \uc2 With data next week expected to show that the Japanese economy didn't expand at all in GDP terms last year, and with net exports still declining in line with the slowdown in the global economy, the last thing Japan is going to need is an even stronger yen at this stage.\par \par \uc2 The fear of a stronger yen has been reflected in persistent warnings from Japanese officials in recent weeks that more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on its way.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Jan Azumi was the latest to do so, asserting that he doesn't rule out any option.\par \par \uc2 Certainly, these warnings are only likely to get more aggressive, especially if Greece's debt talks continue to show little sign of progress.\par \par \uc2 At the moment, global market sentiment is still holding up on hopes that either Greece reaches an early settlement or that any Greek default is ring-fenced.\par \par \uc2 But, if this is not the case, and there is little reason to believe that it is, risk sentiment will fall back sharply and safe havens such as the yen will once again be back in high demand.\par \par \uc2 At that stage, the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  could find it is faced with an even more difficult battle than it had back in October to prevent the yen from rising to new record highs against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 With its reputation at risk and with the Japanese economy at stake, it isn't surprising that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is invoking the Greek deities to come to its rescue.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg TNI FRX POV\par \par \uc2 Reuters USD/DJ\par \par \uc2 Thomson P/1066 or P/1074\par \par \uc2 (Nicholas Hastings is a Senior Correspondent in London for Dow Jones Newswires who has written about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than 20 years. He previously covered a variety of markets, including equities, fixed income, commodities and energy. He can be contacted on +44-20-7842-9493 or by email: nick.hastings@dowjones.com or on twitter @NickHastingsDJ) [ 07-02-12 1113GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1066   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120207e827000xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
