\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Japan says won't rule out more  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  action; confirms stealth  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2012\par 01:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Tokyo will act in \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when needed -Azumi\par \par \uc2 * Tokyo sold Y1 trln in stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Nov -MOF\par \par \uc2 * BOJ Shirakawa signals monetary conditions already loose\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto and Kaori Kaneko\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed up its record yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year with covert \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance minister said it is ready to step in again to counter speculative moves, repeating his strong warning to markets against pushing up the yen too much.\par \par \uc2 The yen crept up near its record high against the dollar hit last October, when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , raising concern among policymakers that renewed yen gains may derail Japan's fragile economic recovery from the damage wrought by last year's earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Jun Azumi said on Tuesday Japan will not rule out any steps to battle speculative moves, repeating his verbal warning of action on hope it will at least keep traders wary of testing the yen's upside for now.\par \par \uc2 "If speculative moves become evident and market moves deviate from economic fundamentals, and speculators distort markets in their self interest, I'll take any steps if necessary in order to protect Japan's national interest," Azumi said.\par \par \uc2 "As I said back then (when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), I would not rule out any measures," he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Data released by the finance ministry the same day confirmed earlier estimates that Tokyo spent roughly 1 trillion yen ($13 billion) in early November on undeclared forays into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The covert action was conducted for four days after the hefty 8 trillion yen unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Oct. 31, to make sure its impact would not fade quickly.\par \par \uc2 The data also showed Tokyo only bought dollars, not euros.\par \par \uc2 "Azumi underlined the fact that the ministry's stance remains unchanged on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is that it will act when necessary despite criticism from Europe and the United States of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's past solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Bank in Tokyo and a former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official.\par \par \uc2 "If the yen's ascent towards these levels become too rapid, that would prompt authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as companies cannot keep up with rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves," he said.\par \par \uc2 BOJ ALSO UNDER PRESSURE\par \par \uc2 Many market players believe Japanese may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again should the dollar fall well below the record low of 75.31 yen, as exporters struggle with a combination of a slowing global economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at around 76.60 yen on Tuesday .\par \par \uc2 Japanese electronics makers have reported huge losses with Panasonic forecasting loss of $10 billion in the financial year to March.\par \par \uc2 But some analysts think Tokyo is more wary of selling the yen heavily after the U.S. Treasury in December chided \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It's uncertain whether Tokyo will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again given criticism from the United States," said Kengo Suzuki, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Mizuho Securities.\par \par \uc2 The yen's renewed strength has also heightened pressure on the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  to ease monetary policy further, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unwilling to loosen credit immediately.\par \par \uc2 BOJ Governor \uc2 Masaaki Shirakawa\uc2  told parliament the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to do its utmost to pull Japan out of deflation, describing the economy as in a severe state.\par \par \uc2 But he added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was already supplying ample funds. The BOJ is expected to stand pat on monetary policy at its next rate review on Feb. 13-14 unless Europe's sovereign debt crisis triggers a severe market turmoil or the yen hits new records.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Oct. 31, Japanese authorities said they needed to act against speculative market moves and that they would continue to act until they were satisfied.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has stayed above the record low since then but crept near that level last month after the U.S. Federal Reserve pledged to keep interest rates low until late 2014. ($1 = 76.6000 Japanese yen)\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Hideyuki Sano and Leika Kihara, writing by Leika Kihara; Editing by Joseph Radford and Tomasz Janowski)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/YEN(UPDATE 2)   \