\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ BLOG/ \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Real Time: Stealth  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 : When Ministers Actin Secret\b0\par\par\uc2 770 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2012\par 11:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's Japan Real Time Report blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/japanrealtime"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/japanrealtime}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 By Takashi Mochizuki\par \par \uc2 Japan's finance ministry confirmed on Tuesday that between Nov. 1 and Nov. 4 last year it conducted 'stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' for the first time in seven years, selling down the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the tune of Y1.0195 trillion -- a cool $13.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 Stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? In the high-octane world of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , JRT has already brought you "The BOJ Rate Check" and "Strong Yen for Dummies", but stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Here's the breakdown.\par \par \uc2 What is stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first place?\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also known as secret \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and its biggest feature is that an authority neither confirms nor denies its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market transactions. In Japan's case for example, Finance Minister Jun Azumi up until yesterday only said "no comment" when asked if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  staged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November. That is a stark contrast to other recent Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigns, which were immediately followed by a finance minister press conference declaring it did.\par \par \uc2 How is it conducted?\par \par \uc2 Usually an authority places orders through a limited number of commercial banks. By doing so, when these orders show up in the market they look like as if they were simply carried out by these commercial banks.\par \par \uc2 But the banks are sworn to secrecy: An agent bank is required to submit a written consent to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  beforehand which contains names of all the people at the bank who will know about the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These people are asked to pledge that they won't tell anyone, even colleagues, whether they received orders from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If the MOF finds out that an agent bank has leaked information, retribution is harsh -- the ministry omits that bank from its list of future potential agent banks. Since serving as an agent bank at a time of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a major money-making opportunity, the threat of being booted off the list is a major deterrent to any leaking. Though the complete list of the MOF's agent banks is not available for public consumption, it is believed most major banks in Tokyo, not only Japanese but also foreign banks, are on there.\par \par \uc2 What is point of conducting stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 The theory is that by shrouding market participants in doubt over what it's up to, a \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  can keep a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a certain level with a relatively small budget. In fact, over the period in question the dollar remained relatively stable at around Y78.00: Data released on Tuesday showed the MOF only spent Y200 billion to Y300 billion a day during the four-day-long \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  period.\par \par \uc2 Publicly announced \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by contrast, usually require a larger budget, one of the most common purposes being to move a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply.\par \par \uc2 For example, on Oct. 31 last year \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. By the end of the day it had spent Y8 trillion -- over $100 billion -- lifting the dollar by more than Y3.\par \par \uc2 How does the market find out about stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's case, the MOF releases quarterly details of daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data retrospectively. So the secret can only be kept for up to three months.\par \par \uc2 But that's fine with the ministry: A three-month period is such a long time for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that it's pretty old news by the time it comes out, and investors won't try to trade on it, moving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders do try to find out about stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  though when they think it's actually taking place, guessing at the Bank of Japan's daily account figures. In November's case, dealers said one commercial bank was selling the yen at a certain level, and the yen didn't rise above that certain level throughout the period. That was just odd enough to make them guess that stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be under way.\par \par \uc2 One last thing to know...\par \par \uc2 While in some countries central banks have the right to decide when to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  that power resides with the finance minister.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is simply an agent which conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the MOF. So calling \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  a BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't quite right. In the strictest sense, it's the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 07-02-12 1036GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120207e827000v5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
