\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Under Pressure After Surprise RBA Decision\b0\par\par\uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2012\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Euro under pressure due to Australian interest rate decision, Greece debt negotiations,\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  data confirms authorities conducted stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  following Oct. 31 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --Greece strikes, \uc2 Fed\uc2 's Bernanke's House appearance eyed for cues\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Alexander Martin \par    Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 )--The euro was under pressure against the dollar and yen during Asian trading Tuesday as a surprise decision by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  to keep its rates unchanged and prolonged uncertainty over Greek debt negotiations pushed down the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The RBA's decision to maintain its benchmark interest rate at 4.25% surprised the market, which had expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cut the rate to 4.00%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar rose sharply after the announcement, reaching a six month high of $1.0811 against the dollar. The surprise move by the RBA meant the euro slid to a record low against the Aussie, trading at A$1.2134.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the euro's fall against the Australian dollar may have dragged the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down against other major peers, including the greenback and yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The focus now will be whether or not the RBA intends to cut rates further in the future," said Daisaku Ueno, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Should demand conditions weaken materially, the inflation outlook would provide scope for easier monetary policy," RBA Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Glenn Stevens\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a statement accompanying the decision, adding that underlying inflation at the end of 2011 was around 2.5%, or in the middle of the bank's target range of 2-3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of 0450 GMT, the euro was at $1.3103, down from $1.3131 in late New York trade on Monday, while it was at Y100.55 from Y100.54, according to trading platform EBS. The dollar was at Y76.69 from Y76.55.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at about 79.183 from about 78.924.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Uncertainty over Greek debt negotiations also lingered, with Greek Prime Minister Lucas Papademos expected to meet today with political leaders in a bid to strike a deal on austerity measures, after skipping talks Monday and failing to wrap up negotiations during the weekend.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Investors may be buying the greenback due to concern over the outcome of the Greece negotiations, said Kengo Suzuki, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Mizuho Securities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the Japanese government released data Tuesday confirming that authorities conducted stealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after its widely publicized Oct. 31 yen selling. Records show it sold Y8.072 trillion on Oct. 31 and Y1.019 trillion over the following four days.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Suzuki of Mizuho Securities said the news may have buoyed the dollar against the yen, although its impact on the market was expected to be limited.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looking ahead, the market is focused on Athens as it braces for strikes that are being called by two major umbrella unions, public sector ADEDY and private sector GSEE, as well as a short-term securities auction later in the day.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke's appearance later before the U.S. House Budget Committee will also be closely watched for cues.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 23:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates                               Close            High      Low  12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            76.68-70       76.53-56  +0.19    76.78    76.52  -0.29 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.3102-04      1.3129-34  -0.22   1.3135   1.3090  +1.10 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.5805-10      1.5820-29  -0.11   1.5830   1.5798  +1.71 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.9205-08      0.9183-88  +0.23   0.9213   0.9186  -1.77 \par USD/CAD Canada          0.9963-68      0.9956-61  +0.07   0.9972   0.9954  -2.39 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.0790-94      1.0724-29  +0.61   1.0807   1.0704  +5.72 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.8339-44      0.8338-43  +0.01   0.8365   0.8330  +7.27 \par  \par Euro Rate \par  \par EUR/JPY Japan           100.48-52      100.46-54  +0.00   100.70   100.38  +0.95 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Alexander Martin, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 813-6269-2783; alexander.martin@dowjones.com [ 07-02-12 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120207e827000d0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
