\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2012\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: TO MAKE UTMOST EFFORT TO COMBAT DEFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa pledged Tuesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will keep making efforts to pull the nation out of long-lasting deflationary pressure. (published 0051 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DATA CONFIRMS MOF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET AFTER OCT 31 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese finance ministry conducted stealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to stem the yen's rise after its highly publicized yen-selling campaign on Oct. 31, data released by the Ministry confirmed Tuesday. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: NO COMMENT ON ISSUE OF STEALTH \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Tuesday he won't rule out any options on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. (published 2356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC SUSPENDS BILL SALE FOR FIFTH STRAIGHT WEEK - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday suspended its routine bill offering for the fifth straight week, signaling Beijing's continued efforts to bolster the economy with liquidity in the money market, traders participating in the open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0140 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER: NO CURRENT PLANS FOR STIMULUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Tuesday reiterated the government currently has no plans to introduce a stimulus package despite slowing growth. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA EXPECTS JANUARY CURRENT-ACCOUNT DEFICIT, SAYS DOMESTIC DEMAND WEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea likely ran a current-account deficit in January for the first time in nearly two years, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Tuesday, as the euro zone sovereign debt crisis sapped global economic momentum. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA REPEATS VOW TO TAME INFLATION EVEN AS GROWTH SLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Ministry of Strategy and Finance on Tuesday repeated its aim to keep inflation in the low-3% region this year, setting price stability as its policy priority even as growth slows. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: PHILIPPINES JAN CPI 3.9% ON YEAR; MARKET EXPECTED 3.9% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines was 3.9% in January, decelerating from 4.2% in December, due mainly to slower increases in beverage and tobacco prices, data released by the National Statistics Office Tuesday showed. (published 0110 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TIGHT BANK CREDIT DAMPS AUSTRALIAN CONSTRUCTION ACTIVITY IN JANUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Restrained bank lending is being blamed for a further fall in Australian construction activity in January, with interest rate cuts late in 2011 only providing slight relief, the Australian Industry Group said Tuesday. (published 2230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : JANUARY CPI PROVIDES POLICY SCOPE TO SUPPORT GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Gov. Amando Tetangco Tuesday said a slower rate of inflation last month provides policy scope to support growth. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NZ TREASURY: OUTLOOK FOR 2012-13 HAS DETERIORATED DUE TO ESCALATION OF EURO AREA CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand Treasury said Tuesday its outlook for 2012-2013 has deteriorated since its pre-election update in late October due to the escalation of the euro area crisis. (published 0127 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA REGULATOR: ACCEPTED FIRST APPLICATION FOR ETF LINKED TO HONG KONG-LISTED SHARES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's securities regulator said late Monday that it has accepted an application to launch the country's first exchange traded fund linked to Hong Kong-listed shares on Feb. 1, marking another small step towards the further opening of the country's tightly-controlled capital account. (published 0115 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: OBAMA TO PRESENT BUDGET PROPOSAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama will release his budget plan on Monday, calling for $3 trillion in deficit reductions over 10 years, including $1.5 trillion in tax increases to fall mostly on the wealthiest Americans. (published 0023 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GERMANY, FRANCE EYE CORPORATE TAX HARMONIZATION -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Governments of Germany and France have agreed to a preliminary framework that would converge their corporate tax structures to avoid double taxation and improve competitiveness of Europe in general, German newspaper Sueddeutsche Zeitung reported on Tuesday, citing people close to the negotiations. (published 0007 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK JAN SAME-STORE SALES FALL AS CONSUMER CAUTION RETURNS - BRC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. retail sales fell on a like-for-like basis in the first month of the new year, in the second-worst January performance since records began in 1995, as consumers returned to a more frugal frame of mind following a busy December. (published 0001 GMT) [ 07-02-12 0200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120207e8270003c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
