\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: Japan Hardens  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Rhetoric As Yen Nears Record High\b0\par\par\uc2 668 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2012\par 03:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- Japan's finance minister hardens \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric after yen hits three-month high against dollar\par \par \uc2 -- Says he can't overlook speculative moves to push yen higher\par \par \uc2 -- Repeats he will take "decisive steps" against yen if needed\par \par \uc2 -- Some analysts doubt \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  without U.S. support\par \par \uc2 (Adds more comments from Japanese government official in 4th paragraph, analyst comments in 8th paragraph, more background throughout) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Nakamichi \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister said Thursday he cannot "overlook" speculative moves in the market to push the yen higher, stepping up his warnings over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's renewed strength as it threatens to exacerbate the nation's trade shortfalls and economic slowdown.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I am calmly watching the market now, but I can't overlook any acceleration in moves by short-term speculators" in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, Jun Azumi told reporters at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "As I have been saying, I will take decisive steps if deemed necessary."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell to Y76.02 Wednesday, the lowest since Oct. 31, when \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  carried out a widely publicized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that sold an estimated daily record of around Y7.5 trillion. There is speculation that without official actions to bolster the dollar, it may soon drop below a record low of Y75.31, also marked on Oct. 31, on expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will continue its loose monetary policy for longer and keep the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weak.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior Japanese government official told Dow Jones Newswires earlier in the day that even though the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has held above Y76.00, he finds its current levels "unpleasant."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen's gains in the face of Japan's economic difficulties strike Japanese officials as economically unreasonable. Recent data have shown that Japan last year posted its first annual trade deficit since 1980, prompting some economists to start arguing that the yen's uptrend should end this year. Japan's consumer prices also fell for the third straight year in 2011 on persistently weak domestic demand.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The current round of yen strength is a major test for Japanese officials.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. and Europe have grown critical of Tokyo's attempts to weaken the yen through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with their own economies needing boosts from exports. But allowing the yen to keep climbing would make Japanese exports less competitive abroad and accelerate Japan's industrial "hollowing" by making manufacturers shift production abroad.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While traders grew wary of Japanese actions, Tohru Sasaki, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JPMorgan Chase Bank, said that "we consider the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  very low" even if the dollar breaks below Y75 given the U.S. Treasury's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  report issued last December.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Treasury report contained a surprisingly strong reprimand against Tokyo's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen in August and October, and argued against Japanese views that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market was disorderly.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sasaki noted that, as the dollar-yen rate is now even less volatile than at the end of October, "it would be difficult (for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) to justify \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " to the U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Public grumbling by U.S. officials could undermine the impact of Japanese action by raising doubts that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be able to continue any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may also need to improve policy communication with the U.S. While the Treasury report caught Japanese officials off guard, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's October \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears to have surprised the U.S. government as well, a person familiar with the issue has told Dow Jones Newswires. Through behind-the-door discussions ahead of that month's yen-selling, Tokyo officials had given their U.S. counterpart the impression that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would hold off on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the person said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; +81-3-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Kosaku Narioka contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February 01, 2012 21:18 ET (02:18 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120202e822000gs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
