\par\par \b \uc2 DJ 2nd UPDATE: BOJ Yamaguchi Says Ctrl Bank Ready To Act, But Immediate Steps On Yen Unlikely\b0\par\par\uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2012\par 07:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- BOJ Deputy Gov. Yamaguchi pledges to take appropriate policy action\par \par \uc2 -- Doesn't think yen's recent rise will trigger immediate steps by BOJ\par \par \uc2 -- Thinks thorough analysis of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trends and their economic impact needed before taking policy steps\par \par \uc2 -- Says he can't rule out possibility that market confidence on sustainability of European monetary union may be hurt\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds comments from press conference in 5th-7th paragraphs)\par \par \uc2 TAKAMATSU, Japan (Dow Jones)--The deputy governor of the Bank of Japan said Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to take action amid growing concerns over the European debt crisis, although he doesn't think the yen's recent rise will trigger immediate policy action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it will take time to judge the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trend and its impact on the economy.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ will "strive to continue to take appropriate policy responses with due recognition that there is a high degree of uncertainty for the time being, including the effects of a slowdown in overseas economies and the appreciation of the yen," Hirohide Yamaguchi told business leaders in Takamatsu, western Japan.\par \par \uc2 Yamaguchi's remarks are likely to add to market expectations that the BOJ would eventually take additional easing measures if further strengthening in the yen-- which already stands near its all-time high against the dollar--weakens Japan's fragile recovery from the on March 11 earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 As of 0640 GMT, the dollar stood at Y76.12, near its all-time low of Y75.31 marked Oct. 31, when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out widely publicized \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that sold an estimated daily record of around Y7.5 trillion.\par \par \uc2 However, Yamaguchi said it requires thorough analysis of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trends and their economic impact before taking any monetary policy action.\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ would consider possible policy responses after carefully examining the impact of the strong yen in Japan on both economic and price front," Yamaguchi told reporters later in the day.\par \par \uc2 He also played down the argument in the markets that the BOJ has been less aggressive than the U.S. Federal Reserve in terms of monetary easing, and that such an attitude contributes to the yen's strength, saying there isn't much difference in their views on prices, as well as commitments to accommodative policy.\par \par \uc2 While recent steps by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other major central banks have helped ease tensions in financial markets, the biggest concern for the global economy remains the euro zone, Yamaguchi said.\par \par \uc2 "We should not lack vigilance about whether a vicious cycle--a problem which has originated on the fiscal front spreads over to the financial front and further to the real economy--will further expand globally," Yamaguchi said.\par \par \uc2 Yamaguchi said the euro zone's problems are partly due to the bloc's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system created by unifying economies with different levels of competitiveness and different fiscal conditions.\par \par \uc2 Yamaguchi said he couldn't rule out the possibility that market confidence in the sustainability of monetary union in the euro zone may be hurt, promising to keep a close eye on such "tail risk."\par \par \uc2 For Japan, Yamaguchi stressed that it is necessary to make efforts on fiscal structural reforms both in terms of expenditure and revenue, in addition to boosting growth potential, before market confidence is lost.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ's policy board decided at its latest meeting in January to leave the unsecured overnight call loan rate in a 0.0%-0.1% range. It also maintained the size of its asset-purchase fund--the BOJ's main tool for credit easing--at Y55 trillion.\par \par \uc2 The bank buys a variety of assets from government and corporate bonds to listed stock and real estate funds via this fund to lower longer-term interest rates and risk premiums.\par \par \uc2 "If such domestic accommodative financial conditions are utilized aggressively for tapping external and domestic demand, I believe Japan's economy can emerge from deflation," Yamaguchi said.\par \par \uc2 -By Megumi Fujikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2786; megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 02, 2012 01:51 ET (06:51 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120202e822001fb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
