\par\par \b \uc2 Data On Feb 7 To Confirm If  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Shifted To "Stealth"  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2012\par 02:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will on Feb. 7 release detailed data on its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the fourth quarter of 2011, a ministry official said Wednesday, figures that will make clear whether Tokyo was covertly active in the market after its highly publicized yen-selling campaign on Oct. 31.\par \par \uc2 The quarterly data, which will be issued at 0850 local time on Feb. 7--or 2350 GMT on Monday, Feb. 6--will provide a daily breakdown of the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the period, along with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs involved. The breakdown will be released, as usual, along with monthly foreign reserves data.\par \par \uc2 At the end of November the ministry released an overall figure for Oct 28-Nov 28, which showed total yen-selling of Y9.092 trillion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data are attracting closer than usual attention from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders.\par \par \uc2 As the MOF tries to rein in a stubbornly strong yen that is damaging the economy, any shift in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics toward "stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " could make it more difficult for investors to predict its actions or forecast the direction of the dollar-yen exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 In November, market participants told Dow Jones Newswires that the MOF appeared to have continued stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for nearly a week after the full-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Oct. 31 that was publicly announced by Finance Minister Jun Azumi.\par \par \uc2 That would be a marked departure from the three previous one-day \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  since September 2010.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com [ 01-02-12 0139GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120201e8210002s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
