\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2012\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA OFFICIAL JANUARY PMI RISES, BEATS EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's official Purchasing Managers Index rose to 50.5 in January from 50.3 in December, the China Federation of Logistics and Purchasing, which issues the data with the National Bureau of Statistics, said in a statement\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC CHINA\f28 \uc2 \f2  JANUARY FINAL PMI 48.8 VS 48.7 IN DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The final \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC China Manufacturing\f28 \uc2 \f2  Purchasing Managers Index, a gauge of nationwide manufacturing activity, rose slightly to 48.8 in January compared with 48.7 in December, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: S KOREA POSTS FIRST TRADE DEFICIT IN 2 YEARS AS GROWTH MOMENTUM STALLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea ran its first trade deficit in two years in January while inflation eased to a one-year low, underscoring slowing economic momentum for the export-dependent country. (published 0242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PM SAYS A$ WILL STAY HIGH FOR YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar will likely stay high for years to come as investors use it to bet on China's growth and as record foreign investment flows into the nation's bonds, Prime Minister Julia Gillard said in a speech Wednesday. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA JAN PERFORMANCE OF MANUFACTURING INDEX +1.4 PTS TO 51.6 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's manufacturing sector grew for the second consecutive month in January but factory output remains constrained by the uncertain global outlook and strong offshore competition, a performance gauge produced by an industry group published Wednesday shows. (published 2230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA ON FEB 7 TO CONFIRM IF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SHIFTED TO "STEALTH" \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will on Feb. 7 release detailed data on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets in the fourth quarter of 2011, a ministry official said Wednesday, figures that will make clear whether Tokyo was covertly active in the market after its highly publicized yen-selling campaign on Oct. 31. (published 0139 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA AVERAGE HOUSING PRICE LOWER IN JANUARY VS DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The average housing price for 100 major cities across China was lower for a fifth consecutive month in January, a China Real Estate Index System survey showed Wednesday. (published 0218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA 4Q HOUSE PRICE INDEX -1.0% VS 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The weighted average price of established houses in Australian capital cities fell 1.0% in the fourth quarter from the third, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said Wednesday. (published 0031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA DECEMBER NEW HOME SALES DOWN 4.9% - HIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New home sales in Australia fell 4.9% in December, according to the Housing Industry Association, drawing on a survey of the country's 100 biggest builders. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NEW ZEALAND HOMES FOR SALE FALLS TO LOWEST LEVEL IN 4 YEARS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of homes for sale in New Zealand's three largest cities has fallen to its lowest level in four years, according to figures released by property website Realestate.co.nz, New Zealand Herald said in a report Wednesday. (published 2014 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TAIWAN \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  JANUARY PMI 48.9 VS 47.1 DECEMBER - MARKIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Taiwan Purchasing Managers Index rose to 48.9 in January from 47.1 in December, as the deterioration in domestic and export orders eased, index compiler Markit Group said Wednesday. (published 0205 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DAH SING BANK SELLS S$225 MLN OF BONDS AT 4.875% YIELD - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dah Sing Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has sold S$225 million worth of subordinated bonds, a person familiar with the matter said Wednesday. (published 0049 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AMERICA MOVIL BOND TO SELL 3-YEAR DIM SUM BOND - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mexico's \f28 \uc2 \f2 America Movil S.A.B. de C.V\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to sell an offshore yuan-denominated bond with a maturity of three years, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Wednesday. (published 0218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par FOCUS: JAPAN HOPES CHINA BOND BUYING WILL SPEED UP MARKET REFORMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When Japanese Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda and his Chinese counterpart Wen Jiabao met in December, a deal by Tokyo to buy Chinese government bonds was hailed by the two as way to bring the major trading partners even closer together. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 01-02-12 0300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120201e8210004y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
