\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 875 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2012\par 13:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU GOVERNMENTS CLOSER TO FISCAL UNION DEAL, EUR500B BAILOUT FUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leaders of 25 European Union governments agreed on what some were billing as a historic pact to move to closer fiscal union and to finally sign off on the details of a EUR500 billion ($660 billion) permanent bailout fund for the euro zone that should come into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at mid-year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JUNCKER: WON'T RULE OUT GREEK HAIRCUT FOR PUBLIC-SECTOR CREDITORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Eurogroup head Jean-Claude Juncker said he won't rule out the possibility that public-sector creditors might also have to forego repayments on their loans to Greece.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 4.0% IN DEC, BEATS FORECASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese industrial production rose 4.0% in December from the previous month, the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Tuesday, as the impact of the flooding in Thailand on Japanese manufacturers began to ease.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMANY ADJ UNEMPLOYMENT AGAIN HITS RECORD LOW IN JAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rapid fall in Germany's seasonally adjusted unemployment figures in January is a signal that the country's economy is on track to recover early this year, after a mild contraction in the fourth quarter of last year, experts say.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN JOBLESS DATA JUSTIFY HOPES FOR GERMAN ECON REBOUND - ECON MIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany's benign labor market justifies hopes that the country's economy will soon return to a growth path, Economics Minister Philipp Roesler said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN RETAIL SALES FALL IN DECEMBER BUT STILL UP IN 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German retail sales fell in December, defying expectations for a rise, but were still higher in the whole of last year as consumer sentiment was buoyed by a strong labor market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH CONSUMER SPENDING ENDS 2011 ON A WEAK NOTE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French household spending dropped sharply and unexpectedly in December, data showed Tuesday, raising questions over French President Nicolas Sarkozy's eleventh hour plan to increase sales taxes in an economy heavily reliant on consumer spending.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ITALY DECEMBER JOBLESS RANKS HIT 11-YEAR HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy's unemployment rate rose to 8.9% in December, with the jobless ranks swelling to their highest level in more than a decade, national statistics institute Istat said Tuesday, citing preliminary data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF SAYS ASIA HAS ROOM FOR STIMULUS IF OUTLOOK DARKENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia has so far proved resilient to the European sovereign-debt crisis and slowing global growth, and countries in the region have room to take growth-boosting steps in case of a sharp downturn, the International Monetary Fund said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TURKEY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ISSUES HAWKISH INFLATION FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday issued a hawkish inflation report, revising its price forecasts sharply higher and stressing that policy should remain tight to counter price pressures and external risks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN AZUMI: TO TAKE DECISIVE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STEPS IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister issued a fresh warning Tuesday that he will take "decisive steps" if speculators push the yen up too sharply, after the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose to its strongest level in around three months overnight.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF SCHIFF: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SHOULD ONLY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF HIGH VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market during periods of high volatility, a senior official at the International Monetary Fund said Tuesday, adding that such action has little lasting effect. the country's growth in gross domestic product for the last fiscal year ended March 31, 2011, to 8.4% from 8.5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA END-SEPTEMBER EXTERNAL FINANCIAL ASSETS TOTALED $4.67 TRILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's total foreign assets came to $4.665 trillion at the end of September, up around 1% from the end of June, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S AUTO EXPORTS -2.1% ON YEAR IN DEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's exports of cars, trucks and buses declined 2.1% on year in December, falling for the first time in five months, as Japanese car makers sought to cut back exports from their home country amid the strong yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S AUTO PRODUCTION +13.4% ON YEAR IN DEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Production of cars, trucks and buses in Japan increased 13.4% on year in December, rising for the third consecutive month, as car makers revved up output with their normalized parts supply chains to make up for lost production after the March earthquake.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PBOC DOESN'T HOLD TUESDAY'S OPEN MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  didn't conduct its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday, in a move apparently aimed at easing tight liquidity conditions in the banking system as a large amount of reverse repurchase agreements will mature this week, traders participating in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: AUSTRALIA'S BANKS WILL FEEL THE SQUEEZE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Home or abroad, Australian banks can't catch a break.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: TOKYO'S FISCAL WOES DON'T LEAD TO ROME \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Comparing Japan to Italy is neat shorthand for measuring the Asian nation's debt load. It's also misleading.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: CHINA JANUARY MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY LIKELY SLOWED - POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's manufacturing activity likely contracted in January after a brief rebound in December, as factories and plants sat idle across the country during the just ended weeklong Lunar New Year holiday, economists said. [ 31-01-12 1202GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120131e81v0014w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
